{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers","id":537689,"title":"[Codename: Sardonyx] - Teasers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-02T20:44:23-07:00","id":537689,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [Codename: Sardonyx] - Teasers","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/codename-sardonyx-teaser-the-first/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/codename-sardonyx-teaser-the-first/\" target=\"_blank\"> [Codename: Sardonyx] Teaser the First &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/codename-sardonyx-teaser-the-first/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/codename-sardonyx-teaser-the-first/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T21:33:17-07:00","id":537729,"title":"","content":"How exciting, however preliminary.<br /> I look forward to reading over this properly tonight when i get an opportunity. Thanks for bringing it up here Ian.<br /> -rubs hands together gleefully-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T21:41:03-07:00","id":537734,"title":"","content":"Here are my first impressions as I read through it:<br /> <br /> - Momentum is interesting. I need to read more about it before I decide whether or not I like it.<br /> - Enhancements seem very interesting. If I understand the concept, the characters' actions and decisions can provide some insurance in case of a bad roll, but won't negate a truly catastrophic roll?<br /> - And if I understand step 5 correctly, an exceptional success can be used to negate a previous failure? Or there's a threshold of success that comes with a Complication, but you can forego the Complication if you roll high enough?<br /> - So excess successes can be used to buy up additional benefits. So far, roll resolution seems extremely versatile. I like it a lot.<br /> - &quot;Rolling dice is fun because it makes the story unpredictable, and influences pacing without the Director just handing down events from on high. It gives players a chance to think about developing strategies and tactics based on the rules.&quot; =&gt; It's always a good sign when the people designing the game understand what the dice are for.<br /> - I don't have much to say on skipping dice rolls. It's meshes together well.<br /> - I'm guessing most of the powers in Trinity and Scion will involve Doubles, increasing Momentum, increasing Enhancements and negating Complications? Maybe turning Consolations into full successes?<br /> - And I just realized that I confused Consolations and Complications during some of my earlier comments?<br /> - The difference between Difficulty and Complications was unclear at first, but the more detailed explanations help a lot.<br /> - &quot;Activate a Power: Some games will include additional ways to spend Momentum. This is a placeholder for those systems.&quot; =&gt; I like that a lot. Not necessarily that momentum can be used to activate powers, but that you've thought about it in advance and laid the necessary foundation.<br /> <br /> Overall, I like it a lot. The basic roll resolution is generic enough that you should be able to adapt it to different subsystems, but it's also complex enough that those subsystems will all feel very different from each other (Compare to a game like Fate, where anything you do comes down to one of four actions and you only have the illusion of distinction.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T23:34:02-07:00","id":537814,"title":"","content":"I'm loving the system! The only real criticism I can come up with is that I don't get why the amount of Momentum you can have in your Black Pool goes down as the Tier goes up. <br /> <br /> That, and may I suggest \u201cFortune\u201d and \u201cTrouble\u201d instead of \u201cBlack\u201d and \u201cRed\u201d?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T00:48:08-07:00","id":537876,"title":"","content":"I am optimistic. I'm concerned a bit about how valuable the black/red pools will be in play; esp. as the black pool is shared amongst the players. It seems a potential point of player style conflict (some players cooperatively managing a shared resource butting up against players trying to contribute as little as possible and grab and free momentum whenever they can. But it's way to early to know exactly how these things will work. I also generally get worried when the Director has to manage a resource to do part of their role in the game. I don't want to get stuck wishing I'd have one more red Momentum for something but not having it and either having to let something potentially fun/interesting go or fudge it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=537734#post537734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Enhancements seem very interesting. If I understand the concept, the characters' actions and decisions can provide some insurance in case of a bad roll, but won't negate a truly catastrophic roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given they don't come in until after you succeed or fail, I think the point is to help the issue the previous games had where 5 successes above what you needed was supposed to be the best a human could do, and then trying to figure out how to make sense of what to do with 20 successes. You might not be able to spend more than 5 successes on &quot;quality of success&quot; effects, but you'll have other effects to boost if you're tossing around enhancements that start hitting really large numbers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - And if I understand step 5 correctly, an exceptional success can be used to negate a previous failure? Or there's a threshold of success that comes with a Complication, but you can forego the Complication if you roll high enough? </div> </div> </div>My reading of this was the later: you can buy off Complications if you roll well enough. Like, you have to make a deal with a mob boss, and he'll expect a favor in return for whatever you're getting from him (Complication) but if you roll really well on your roll to make the deal, you can opt to buy off the Complication over spending successes on, say, increasing how big your cut of the deal is going to be; convincing the mobster that the deal is beneficial enough that they're going to not demand a favor after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - I'm guessing most of the powers in Trinity and Scion will involve Doubles, increasing Momentum, increasing Enhancements and negating Complications? Maybe turning Consolations into full successes? </div> </div> </div>My guesses are that Momentum is going to be a mixed resource regarding powers; some powers will generate it, others spend it, depending on what they do and who they benefit/harm. I'd also imagine part of this framework system is that powers will largely focus on letting you do things normal Attribute + Ability combos can innately do over dice mechanic adjustments (at least for higher tiers). So low tiers get dice mechanic tricks that give them some edges and what not. Medium and upper tiers are doing things like eye-lasers and flying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=537814#post537814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm loving the system! The only real criticism I can come up with is that I don't get why the amount of Momentum you can have in your Black Pool goes down as the Tier goes up.<br /> <br /> That, and may I suggest \u201cFortune\u201d and \u201cTrouble\u201d instead of \u201cBlack\u201d and \u201cRed\u201d?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing that pool sizes going down with Tier is part of the scaling structure; especially for mixed tier play. High tier characters probably don't need a few bonus dice, or giant piles of momentum to do what they need to do. But having momentum is still useful. This creates a reason to bring lower tier characters along, since they increase the maximum size of the group's pool (and even if a bit out classed, if they fail a lot they generate momentum/aids that way). A command/leadership focused higher tier character could manage to really boost the rolls of a lower tier henchmen without a lot of extra powers to handle that.<br /> <br /> I'm also thinking the names of the pools will be adjusted to the different game lines. I'm not sure calling the red pool specifically something negative is a good idea, since I was getting the idea that it could be used to boost friendly NPCs as well as antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T05:08:46-07:00","id":538080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=537814#post537814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm loving the system! The only real criticism I can come up with is that I don't get why the amount of Momentum you can have in your Black Pool goes down as the Tier goes up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Target number decreases as Tier increases; more powerful characters don't fail quite as often. They've also got supernatural fuel traits to balance things out. But as others have noted, it's quite modular, so we can fiddle with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T05:15:41-07:00","id":538082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also thinking the names of the pools will be adjusted to the different game lines. I'm not sure calling the red pool specifically something negative is a good idea, since I was getting the idea that it could be used to boost friendly NPCs as well as antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>It surely can, so the Director can indirectly aid if she wants. <br /> <br /> They're black and red because sardonyx is black and red, but different names is something to consider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T10:59:27-07:00","id":538555,"title":"","content":"Just adding my voice to those thanking the team for getting this out to us. Its really appreciated <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Having read it through a couple of times now here's how my thoughts have settled:<br /> <br /> <b>Likes</b><br /> <br /> * Base system (x+y)<br /> * Fixed target number<br /> * Fixed target numbers tied to tiers<br /> * Double 10s's (yes!)<br /> * Mentioning options for dice, no dice, agreement play etc. Each to their own but its nice to have it spelled out, especially for newbies<br /> * No modifying of dice pools<br /> <br /> <b>Too Early To Tell</b><br /> <br /> * Enhancements - not enough info<br /> * Complications / Buying off complications - seems cumbersome at face value<br /> * Effects could go either way, depends on the implementation. Could be very cool, or cumbersome - need more info<br /> * Mixed actions - not enough info really<br /> * No modifying of target numbers<br /> <br /> <b>Dislikes*</b><br /> <br /> * Consolations and Momentum. Seems like a bunch of additional work right at points in a game when things are better served by streamlining, in my experience. Feels like a solution in search of a problem<br /> * Black / Red pools - yeah, no way am I keeping up with that. Really dislike this. Also feels like a solution in search of a problem<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: I realize the points I dislike are core the entire new system - so that's a bit of an issue for me personally. Hopefully getting a chance to see more detail and a bit of play-testing will help change my mind on these items. But that's my initial reaction anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":232,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","user":"CHILL","date":". 06-03-2015, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T13:08:00-07:00","id":538697,"title":"","content":"Having played Fate, various Cortex Plus games (Smallville, Leverage, Marvel Superheroes), and similar games of a style I like to call narrative-driven, I think I get where Sardonyx is coming from. <br /> <br /> Several of the games I described above have what I call a \u201cno, but\u2026\u201d mechanism in them. The purpose is to help shift the players' mindset from failure never being an option \u2014 something to be avoided at all costs \u2014 to failure being a detour, something that's still not as <i>good</i> as success but still worthwhile. Sure, I'd love to drive straight through to my destination; but if I can't, I'd rather be put on a detour that leads me around the obstacle than to be stranded by the obstacle (in a chase scene, this might be literally the case). Consolations give the Director a means of rewarding the player for <i>making the attempt</i> even though he didn't get what he was going for, which tends to make the players less risk-averse. <br /> <br /> Likewise, several of these systems have a metagaming currency that the GM is supposed to use to encourage players to go along with plot developments that they would not otherwise be inclined to go along with; that's Momentum. The idea is to encourage the players to have their characters take risks by ensuring that no matter how bad the results are for the <i>character</i>, the <i>player</i> gets something tangible out of it. If you get caught by a roadblock and there's no detour readily available, it still wasn't <i>completely</i> pointless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T13:24:02-07:00","id":538711,"title":"","content":"Funnily, I designed Momentum specifically because of some issues I see with recent games like those. These are:<br /> <br /> 1) Failing &quot;forward&quot; is often accused of making success seem arbitrary and unimportant. It doesn't have to be, but in many, many cases this is what play groups default to.<br /> 2) The trouble with treating every action as an unambiguous move forward in the story is that it threatens to break things down into small pieces, like serving you a cake one crumbly bit at a time.<br /> <br /> Momentum rewards punctuation in performance, rising tension and biding your time. That's why you always spend big. The basic inspiration is the common gambler's fallacy that certain results have to eventually stop happening because they happened before. Momentum makes that fallacy true--your ship will come in--but how big the ship is depends on the risks you're willing to take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":164,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","user":"Malcolm","date":". 06-03-2015, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T14:34:33-07:00","id":538803,"title":"","content":"If it makes you feel any better, Malcom, that's how I read it. I've been Storytelling/DM/GMing almost exclusively for nearly 15 years now, and bumping into the same issues I <i>think </i>your referring to I'm excited about the idea even if (as of now) it seems like a bit more paperwork","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T15:35:39-07:00","id":538855,"title":"","content":"From the teaser post: &quot;So rather than try to hack one system that was originally created for horror gaming into three separate tiers of power, Rich asked us to come up with something that scales properly to all three, and was built with an action focus in mind.&quot; -- THIS. ALL OF THIS.<br /> <br /> To be more specific, there's a quote in Mage's Book of Worlds at the beginning of an Archangel's description (I want to say Gabriel): &quot;Contain yourself! This is one who <i>cannot be fought.&quot;</i> (The Phantom Stranger, referring to the Spectre -- the literal Wrath of God.) No stats. You fight an Archangel, you lose, and what happens next depends on how generous the angel/ST is feeling. That, to me, is quintessential WoD: Some beings simply <i>cannot be challenged,</i> and must be accepted as beyond even godlike reality warpers.<br /> <br /> In Scion? You get to punch the evil creators of the universe <i>in the face</i> and put them back in their hole. That's a viable endgame -- I ran that, too, and it was a blast. A Node 10 Nova? Can <i>create a universe.</i> Not a Horizon Realm (with years/decades of work and a few dozen close personal Archmaster friends), not a world, not a galaxy -- <i>a universe.</i> There's an ongoing cross-game joke that Green Sun King of the Primordials in Exalted is Divis Mal post-retirement. (And wow, did <i>that</i> go wrong if true. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) So, IMO, this is really the right way to go, in theory. We'll find out how it works in practice soon, hopefully.<br /> <br /> EDIT: On a crunchier note, three of the Attributes appear to be Might, Reason and Cunning. Anyone notice others? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":2434,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","user":"Captain Aeon","date":".  Further commentary 06-03-2015, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T16:11:06-07:00","id":538888,"title":"","content":"I like that Complications can be bought off by successes, or left as they are. So you can choose to succeed but maybe suffer the effect of the complication, or fail but resolve the complication, and if there are multiple complications then you can potentially buy off one and still succeed, thus meaning players can pick what complications to resolve and such.<br /> <br /> Seems quite interesting and tactical, and also means that complications are something players can deal with if they spend to resources to do so. Quite a lot of potential outcomes to a single roll, which is good, but it doesn't seem overly complex and has a nice step by step process to work things out. The fact that the Director doesn't have to worry about positives an negatives to dice pools, just setting difficulties and adding complications, means that the mechanic players need to worry about and those the GM need to worry about are pleasantly distinct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T17:56:58-07:00","id":538971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Aeon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=538855#post538855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: On a crunchier note, three of the Attributes appear to be Might, Reason and Cunning. Anyone notice others? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is it sad that I've already been working on a mock up Character sheet based on that alone... don't answer... I already know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T19:10:59-07:00","id":539050,"title":"","content":"Attributes include Might, Reason, Cunning, and Persuasion, in a Physical/Mental/Social by Power/Control/Resistance grid. Might is most likely Physical Power. The others I'm shaky enough to commit to, but I suspect Reason is Mental Power and Cunning is Mental Control. Persuasion seems more Social Control but it could be Power. I don't know if all the Attributes will be differently named or not. I'm hoping they may avoid the somewhat gooey area that is Resolve and Composure in new World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Abilities seem to include Culture, Enigmas, Brawl (the classic returns), and Awareness. It's good that there seems to be a dedicated perceptive skill; I think games tend to suffer without it. I'm curious whether we will have a fixed skill list or not. Also specialties will be a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My guesses are that Momentum is going to be a mixed resource regarding powers; some powers will generate it, others spend it, depending on what they do and who they benefit/harm. I'd also imagine part of this framework system is that powers will largely focus on letting you do things normal Attribute + Ability combos can innately do over dice mechanic adjustments (at least for higher tiers). So low tiers get dice mechanic tricks that give them some edges and what not. Medium and upper tiers are doing things like eye-lasers and flying. </div> </div> </div>I would suggest that powers that actively manipulate Momentum are rare, as it isn't a real, tangible thing in the game worlds, but a narrative conceit. I also don't see Momentum being used for flying and eye lasers. I think powers that call for the expenditure of Momentum will be things like finishers, criticals, combos, limit breaks, overcharges, showstoppers or whatever you want to call them; powers that you can really only use at a certain dramatic point. It would certainly be good for things like &quot;wild talent&quot; - say a psion's power suddenly jumps when trying to keep her daughter from being killed by an Aberrant.<br /> <br /> Actually, you know what would make an excellent Edge? Loved Ones, people you care about who would give you extra Momentum when they are threatened, or when they cheer you on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T19:14:43-07:00","id":539052,"title":"","content":"<i>Red...the dice of angry men...<br /> Black...the games of decades past...<br /> Red...a new system soon to dawn!<br /> Black...a game revived at last!</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T20:23:10-07:00","id":539125,"title":"","content":"Is it bad that I had a similar thought when I first read the spoiler? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T01:52:19-07:00","id":539361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=539050#post539050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm hoping they may avoid the somewhat gooey area that is Resolve and Composure in new World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm seriously hoping not. To me those attributes complete and define the mental and social resistance perfectly. And when you are going to fight high appearance, high manipulation beings, those two attributes start to become essential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T03:48:14-07:00","id":539404,"title":"","content":"Alright, let's break this down.<br /> <br /> <b>Basic Dice Mechanic</b><br /> <br /> As I understand the dice mechanics, they work thus: I form a pool of dice from Attribute + Ability. These are typically standard pools (&quot;Charisma + Presence, Manipulation + Persuasion, Dex + Firearms&quot;) like in the Aeon games, and I presume they are made up of stats that are between 1 and 5, so we'll typically see pools of 1-10.<br /> <br /> Every die that comes up 8+ is a &quot;success.&quot; 10s count double. I spend my successes &quot;on the difficulty&quot; or on &quot;extra effects.&quot; If I do not have enough successes to match/exceed the difficulty, I fail. If I have enough successes to exceed the difficulty, I succeed and if I have any successes at all, I add any &quot;enhancements&quot; I have as successes. I can spend additional successes on effects, which include things like buying off complications or improving effect. If I fail and roll any 1s, I botch and something terrible happens. If I fail or botch, I gain momentum.<br /> <br /> <b>Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> This is excellent! When I was tinkering with a &quot;It's not world of darkness&quot; system for a homebrew, I came up with a few similar concepts for similar reasons (I'm not accusing people of stealing ideas here, just noting that I came to similar conclusions, which makes me think I understand some of the reasoning). This system creates a bell-curve. I like bell-curves. Most of my favorite systems (GURPS, Fate, Exalted) have bell-curves.<br /> <br /> I like to use <a href=\"http://anydice.com/\" target=\"_blank\">AnyDice</a> for my calculations. I'm using the following for my calculations:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> function: sardonyx DICE tn TN double DOUBLE{<br /> COUNT: 0<br /> COUNT: COUNT + [count {TN..10} in DICEd10]<br /> COUNT: COUNT + [count {DOUBLE..10} in DICEd10]<br /> result: COUNT<br /> }<br /> output [sardonyx 10 tn 8 double 10] </div> </div> </div>Just change the value after &quot;sardonyx&quot; for the number of dice, the TN to change the target number, and the double to change the value at which doubles begin to occur (so if it's 8 dice with a TN of 6 and the dice double at 7, you'd change the output to &quot;output [sardonyx 8 tn 6 double 7]&quot; It takes a little bit to calculate, be patient.<br /> <br /> So, what does 10 dice with TN 8 and double 10s look like? It looks like this:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/VrPAXqo.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Anydice went to 20, but it hit 0% at that point. See that beautiful bell-curve? Here's why I think it matters: humans are irrational creatures, something gambling casinos often take advantage of. We expect the ordinary to happen more often than the extraordinary, regardless of what the actual odds are. You see this often in d20 games: People intuitively expect 10 to turn up more often than 20 or 1, but all three results have the same percentage result: 5%. We know, mathematically, that this is true (d20 percentages are super-easy to calculate, one reason why they are popular), but in our heart of hearts, we're often still surprised when this actually happens. A bell-curve eliminates this. It makes the average... average, and the extraordinary, extraordinary.<br /> <br /> That said, this particular system plays havoc with certain expectations. The more I look at it, the more I think it's a feature rather than a bug, and might actually be intentional.<br /> <br /> What are the chances for success on 2 dice? In my heart of hearts, I would guess &quot;Well, about 50%, right?&quot; It should be effectively the toss of the coin. The actual results are:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/ntDiQC8.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/nN5PUyb.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Z6fjSlI.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The above assumes that each tier reduces the TN by one. At TN 8, our average number of successes is actually 0.8. At TN 7, we get the expected average of 1 success, and at TN 6, we actually get 1.2 successes. If we extrapolate this forward, we can see that the system roughly gives you 0.4 successes per die at TN 8, 0.5 at 7, and 0.6 at 6, which is hardly surprising.<br /> <br /> But players aren't machines. They don't roll them bones and then go &quot;Aha, 0.4 successes per die plus or minus a small variance, quite right!&quot; they say &quot;Oh man, I hope I succeed. I should have about X chance...&quot; At TN 8, the &quot;low-level&quot; tier, they're actually slightly wrong in their calculation and they're slightly more likely to fail than they think they are. The dice hate them a little. At the God-tier of TN 6, they're slightly wrong in their calculations and they're more likely to succeed than they think they are. The dice love them a little. The result is that for a mere mortal, the world keeps taking that unexpected little bit from you. There's always that little bit you didn't account for. You might still succeed, but it always costs you a little more than you expected. At the God-Tier, though, the world parts before you. Things are always a little cheaper for you, things just &quot;go your way.&quot;<br /> <br /> If this is how it works, this pleases me. There's a little mathematical slight of hand that I think the average player will miss, but enjoy nonetheless. It's like a magic trick. It's neat.<br /> <br /> But how does it run?<br /> <br /> <b>Dude, where's my dice?</b><br /> <br /> One thing that stands out to me from that design document is how often the writer says &quot;Don't do this! Don't do that!&quot; Some people don't like limitations, but I Iove them. By clearly defining boundaries, we can focus on what we want to matter, and this document does this well. The first problem I often run into a game is how it handles my mistakes. Here's a common mistake: See if it's ever happened to you:<br /> <br /> GM: &quot;Okay! The door bursts in and gullets start flying everywhere as three goons bust in! What do you do?&quot;<br /> Player: &quot;Oh crap! I shoot back!&quot;<br /> GM: &quot;Roll Dex + Firearms!&quot;<br /> Player: &quot;Sweet, I got 3 successes!&quot;<br /> Player 2: &quot;Wait, didn't you just say it was dark?&quot;<br /> GM: &quot;Oh, that's right...&quot;<br /> <br /> What do you do?<br /> <br /> In GURPS, I would say &quot;Oh, right, add -3. Do you still succeed?&quot; And the player might say &quot;I have Night Vision 1&quot; and I would say &quot;Oh, then -2 instead of -3,&quot; and we'd move on.<br /> In Fate, I would say &quot;Oh, sure. That's a scene Aspect.&quot; And I could give him a token to apply a -2 or a reroll, if I wanted. Or I could just ignore it.<br /> In new World of Darkness, though, and in many pool-based games, I have a problem. He needs to lose 2 dice from his pool. &quot;Unroll 2 dice!&quot; I would want to say, but I cannot. So he has to reroll the whole pool. Oh, but I forgot that he has night vision +1! So go ahead and add +1 die. Oh wait, but what about the fact that he's still wounded at -1? So reroll at -1 die... It's terrible. So terrible, in fact, that most nWoD games I've played simply ignore the dice penalties. The GM just says &quot;Roll Dex + Firearms&quot; and ignores all bonuses or penalties and just uses it as a sort of narrative guide.<br /> <br /> Here, we're back to the GURPS/Fate model, again: &quot;Oh, right, add +1 difficulty.&quot; &quot;Okay, then, 2 successes.&quot; And we're good.<br /> <br /> I find that difficulty is best when it's negotiable. If we can fuss back and forth with half-remembered rules or a GM's gut-feeling, then we have a pretty solid system. This allows that.<br /> <br /> <b>Dude, that sucks!</b><br /> <br /> Failure happens. The point of a die-mechanic is to inject the unexpected into the game. There are lots of ways to play with that uncertainty, but the most common is a success/failure matrix: You attempt to do something, to make an impact on the world, and you either succeed or you fail. The problem with these mechanics is that the player conjures up an interesting set of imagery and then attempts to apply that, and the dice sometimes say &quot;Nope!&quot;<br /> <br /> Denied. No cool imagery for you. In fact, nothing. <i>Nothing happened</i>. You whiffed.<br /> <br /> It happens a lot in D&amp;D and one of my players would throw up his hands and say &quot;I hate it when I wasted my turn.&quot; Indeed, we all do. Other systems, like nWoD, make the results so bland that while you seldom fail, your success doesn't much matter (&quot;Oh! This turn I do one damage instead of zero. If I'm lucky, next turn, I might do TWO damage! Woo!&quot;) They replace &quot;whiff&quot; with &quot;whittle&quot; which I would argue is even LESS interesting/dynamic than whiff.<br /> <br /> These mechanics have neither problem. Enhancements ensure that if you &quot;hit,&quot; you can hit <i>hard</i>. Consolation ensures that if you fail, then at least something goes your way, and you didn't &quot;waste your turn.&quot; And the existence of botches ensures that the injection of the unexpected remains.<br /> <br /> Say your character is SUPER-HOT, and you need to get access to a secure facility, and your approach of choice is to waggle your eyebrows at the facility's lonely secretary who's at a club tonight and see if you can &quot;get close enough&quot; to get her access pass. This might be a Manipulation + Seduction roll, but you get your Appearance of +2 as an enhancement: If you succeed, you'll really succeed. You can spend successes on all kinds of bonuses that might make the result of that action terribly interesting. If you fail, then you might be able to pass a little success on to your wingman who can suddenly show up and &quot;rescue her&quot; from your clumsy advances, or perhaps you can notice, when she's thrown that water in your face and stalked off, that she doesn't even have the access pass on her (she probably left it at the coat check. You could break in...). You might even botch (&quot;Bouncer! BOUNCER! Throw this man out!&quot;) but consolation remains in place, so if you learn something vital about security concerns, your larger goal (to break into the installation) might advance a touch, even if you were humiliated in your attempt.<br /> <br /> This means that the game never has to shut down over a bad roll, that the player always has a sense of moving forward.<br /> <br /> <b>Dude, check out my build!</b><br /> <br /> The next element that I find important in games are the ability to have <i>interesting builds</i>. A game, according to Sid Meier, is &quot;A series of interesting choices.&quot; When it comes to RPGs, that often means a series of interesting decisions regarding how you're going to apply your mechanics to overcome a particular challenge. This needs to involve more decisions than just &quot;How do I get as many dice as I can?&quot; though that can have interesting implications (how Willpower interacts with Virtue and Vice in nWoD can create some interesting dynamics, though I seldom see them truly utilized to their full potential). Ideally, we'd have some <i>funky mechanics</i> that work a little differently, or even better, we'd have a <i>system of funky mechanics</i> that work to create a unique structure of mechanical themes that the player can explore.<br /> <br /> Everyone knows this, but the problem is that they're often badly executed. The developer throws a pile of ideas on the fire and says &quot;Sweeeet! This'll be fun!&quot; but doesn't think through the implications. This can create player traps. A good example of this was the alternate willpower mechanics in Hunter: the Vigil, where you could switch out the +3 for 9-again, only this was almost never a good idea (you needed something like 30 dice before it became more worthwhile). This set of mechanics doesn't seem to have that problem (though we have yet to see implementation).<br /> <br /> I've already touched on Enhancements. Let's look at another: Complications. Complications are bad things that can happen to you even if you succeed. Perhaps there's a security camera at an installation you're trying to break into, and a silent alarm, and a late night security guard. If you're breaking in, defeating the silent alarm is a minimum (it would mean a near-instant game-over, since the police would be there in but a few turns). The guard might be an additional complication: If he hears you, he might come to investigate and you'll have to deal with him. The camera won't alert anyone, but it'll mean they'll have your face on tape. If you roll Dex + Stealth and get 2 successes, then you can eliminate two of these three problems. Which do you pick? OOOO an INTERESTING CHOICE! Dun dun dun!<br /> <br /> We can even build this into our character strategies. We might have the ability, success or fail, to bypass one complication no matter what. We might apply automatic complications to our opponents, or we might apply complications to OURSELVES. Imagine a fighter build where, as long as you have any defense available, you apply a &quot;Riposte&quot; complication to any attack made against you, which sets up a counter attack if your opponent doesn't attack more carefully. A well-armored character might ignore it, while a dextrous character might go ahead and pick apart your riposte defense, but they have to deal with it somehow. Perhaps you have a Feint complication on your attacks: If your opponent doesn't eliminate that additional complication with his defense pool, you double your momentum against him. Perhaps you have an Overreach complication on your attack: you get a huge enhancement to your damage, but if you don't eliminate the complication (hit or miss!) you'll add an attack enhancement to any attacks made against you. Oh, you scored only one success on your overreach attack. Are you going to buy off the complication,or hit?<br /> <br /> Then we start to see builds emerge: A dextrous character who excels at ripostes and feints and powerful character who can inflict prodigious damage at a risk to himself, which he compensates for by being well-armored. The dextrous character's ripostes won't do much against that armor, but his feints can start to add up, so he'll make lots of little attacks not with the intent of hitting, but with the intent of building momentum that he can add up into a single, powerful strike that penetrates his opponent's armor and destroy him. The armored character is going to simply ignore most of this and barrel through the deft attacks, taking increasingly desperate risks in an effort to penetrate that defense and land ONE SINGLE HIT. Who will win?<br /> <br /> I don't know, but it'd be more interesting to watch that play out than the typical nWoD fight, or many D&amp;D fights, thanks to the combination of complication, momentum and botches.<br /> <br /> <b>The Dude Abides</b><br /> <br /> A die mechanic is not enough to judge an entire system. Implementation must be good. Exalted has a pretty good die-mechanic, but bad Charm design and some setting problems damaged the brand. I find the core D&amp;D mechanic rather meh, but the implementation of powers and tricks in many iterations of it make up for some of those problems. But what I do see is this: A lot of careful thought was put into this mechanic. It is not over-engineered. It is simple and elegant and easy to implement. It addresses some fairly common problems. It thinks its way through some of its own implications (hence its many pieces of advice). If this level of thought is placed into implementation as well, we should have a pretty good system.<br /> <br /> I loved the Aeon games, and just the other day I found myself discussing it in fond terms. I also really wanted to like Scion, but the game was just not up to par. That this system is being applied to Scion and Aeon fills me with hope. It means a steady hand is at the till.<br /> <br /> <b>Post Script: </b>Your forum software won't allow me to add attachments and shakes its fist at me when I try. Then when I remove said offending pictures and attempt to include them via link instead, it still shakes its fist at me. Deleting everything and trying with a new post doesn't work. Trying to refresh the page to see if that works. Seems to have. Trying to add the pics back in as links... Worked. Thanks for your patience","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6261,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6261-mailanka","user":"Mailanka","date":". 06-04-2015, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6261-mailanka","name":"Mailanka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T09:38:55-07:00","id":539658,"title":"","content":"This is one of the most impressive First Posts I've ever seen, Mailanka. Well done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T09:47:49-07:00","id":539668,"title":"","content":"I think the new system is looking amazing!<br /> <br /> I love how players can work together to help each other succeed. I love the momentum system, as well. I love being able to have very fast, or very drawn-out combat scenes. That's something that has been needed for White Wolf/Onyx Path games for a long time. <br /> <br /> Consolations? My group and I have been doing that for a long time, anyway. It sucks to just completely fail when you're trying to do something cool, so I've always been the kind of ST who will throw his players a bone.<br /> <br /> I'm not as mechanically savvy as others in this forum, but what I'm seeing here, I'm really liking. <br /> <br /> Lookin' forward to seeing more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T10:41:07-07:00","id":539717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=538555#post538555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just adding my voice to those thanking the team for getting this out to us. Its really appreciated <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Having read it through a couple of times now here's how my thoughts have settled:<br /> <br /> <b>Likes</b><br /> <br /> * Base system (x+y)<br /> * Fixed target number<br /> * Fixed target numbers tied to tiers<br /> * Double 10s's (yes!)<br /> * Mentioning options for dice, no dice, agreement play etc. Each to their own but its nice to have it spelled out, especially for newbies<br /> * No modifying of dice pools<br /> <br /> <b>Too Early To Tell</b><br /> <br /> * Enhancements - not enough info<br /> * Complications / Buying off complications - seems cumbersome at face value<br /> * Effects could go either way, depends on the implementation. Could be very cool, or cumbersome - need more info<br /> * Mixed actions - not enough info really<br /> * No modifying of target numbers<br /> <br /> <b>Dislikes*</b><br /> <br /> * Consolations and Momentum. Seems like a bunch of additional work right at points in a game when things are better served by streamlining, in my experience. Feels like a solution in search of a problem<br /> * Black / Red pools - yeah, no way am I keeping up with that. Really dislike this. Also feels like a solution in search of a problem<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: I realize the points I dislike are core the entire new system - so that's a bit of an issue for me personally. Hopefully getting a chance to see more detail and a bit of play-testing will help change my mind on these items. But that's my initial reaction anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is _exactly_ how I see it. Except: I am not sure about the dislikes. I'll have to try how this works in actual gameplay. But I am very sceptical about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1138-dailor","name":"dailor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T11:51:00-07:00","id":539774,"title":"","content":"I am enjoying the system so far from the sneak peek. It gives a ton of possibilities for the ST to go &quot;Yeah, this is happening and this and this and this. How are you going to deal with it?&quot; and then the players get to go &quot;We are taking care of that and that and maaaaaaybe that.&quot; and if they do not handle it all? Then they STILL walk away with something.<br /> Players, even though there is no condition, want to WIN at something when those dice hit the table. This results in them always getting something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T12:02:58-07:00","id":539783,"title":"","content":"Im going to make it rain on the Aeon kickstarters so hard, Noah would have flashbacks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T13:14:17-07:00","id":539903,"title":"","content":"And God'll be like &quot;Woah, dude, let up a bit!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T13:51:10-07:00","id":539946,"title":"","content":"Mailanka, Your post was a great deal of fun to read and what I'm about to say I say with nothing but admiration and respect.<br /> <br /> YOU ARE SUCH A NERD!<br /> <br /> I hope to see more of your nerdery here on the Forum. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T15:11:23-07:00","id":540029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=539774#post539774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Players, even though there is no condition, want to WIN at something when those dice hit the table. This results in them always getting something.</div> </div> </div> </div>*twitch* Don't take this the wrong way, but I have a real issue with this sentiment. I look for a good experience in games, not to win. Some of the best gaming experiences I've seen around the table come from completely and utter failure - especially from unfavorable dice rolls. <br /> <br /> I guess one of the other reasons why I'm really hesitant on the momentum mechanics (apart from my concerns about it adding unneeded admin to a game) is that it appears designed so there's always some kind of 'win' which kinda bugs me. 'Losing' is just a character building opportunity <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, Mailanka. Wow. As someone who really doesn't care at all for that level of analysis of mechanics (I glossed over most of ti), I can still recognize the effort that took. Seriously - nicely done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T15:19:08-07:00","id":540042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=540029#post540029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*twitch* Don't take this the wrong way, but I have a real issue with this sentiment. I look for a good experience in games, not to win. Some of the best gaming experiences I've seen around the table come from completely and utter failure - especially from unfavorable dice rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>The failures still happen. They just add to the PCs' momentum (hence the name), because this is high adventure with heroes (the sort that stop tyrants and killers, not the sort from Beast), and those heroes always save the day in the end. None of this will stop them from paying prices, from the small to the epic, in the process.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T15:43:56-07:00","id":540087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Aeon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=540042#post540042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The failures still happen. They just add to the PCs' momentum (hence the name), because this is high adventure with heroes (the sort that stop tyrants and killers, not the sort from Beast), and those heroes always save the day in the end. None of this will stop them from paying prices, from the small to the epic, in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of the reasoning presented so far behind the mechanics, I just don't agree with it or the implementation. I think a half-decent GM shouldn't let the characters fail (in the sense of dice rolls goes south, the bad guys win, game over). There's no reason I can see to weigh down a game with mechanics for this - it feels restrictive and cumbersome as presented.<br /> <br /> As for 'high adventure with heroes'. That depends on your style preference really so it may be worth considering that not everyone is looking for high adventure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. <br /> <br /> For example my Aeon games would never intended to be and wouldn't be classed as high adventure (note I have no interest in the Adventure! or Aberrant settings, which I'll grant tone may work for). My campaigns have more in common with the.....well, parts of the Dune series or the movie 'Aliens' I guess.<br /> <br /> Tone aside, I'm really still not seeing what need this fills. I'm concerned that by the time we get to a completed setting book (say Aeon) with all the various powers types you have a lot to run through in combat. I'm not suggesting OPP should be abstract to the point of Fate (which is too far the other way for me), but this feels like too much. <br /> <br /> As I've said, I am looking forward to playtesting even though I'm not a fan so far of momentum etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T15:54:23-07:00","id":540098,"title":"","content":"The whole &quot;fail forward&quot; has never been something I've liked either, but this feels somewhat different from failing forward. It more feels like failing giving you an incentive to try different things, and also can drive the game forward. It also makes players more likely to try risky moves in fights and stuff, which often they don't do in my experience because you don't tend to get much from it. I mean, I'm ambivalent about it right now, but as long as it doesn't take the tension out of making a tricky roll, I think I'll be okay. The trouble with failing forward is that essentially it makes the player decisions unimportant as regardless of what happens you succeed, and I dunno if the Sardonyx system has that problem yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T16:03:39-07:00","id":540106,"title":"","content":"Let's put it this way: Sardonyx isn't so much \u201cfail forward\u201d as \u201cfail sideways\u201d: instead of the narrative stopping or even regressing, it twists. <br /> <br /> As for \u201ca halfway decent GM wouldn't let those bad things happen anyway\u201d, true. But then, a halfway-decent GM can make lemonade out of lemons. That doesn't mean that the system desiers should feel content handing him lemons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T16:23:39-07:00","id":540124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=540106#post540106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's put it this way: Sardonyx isn't so much \u201cfail forward\u201d as \u201cfail sideways\u201d: instead of the narrative stopping or even regressing, it twists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must be having very different gaming experiences - why would narrative stop or regress without a fail-forwards (or sideways) system?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=540106#post540106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for \u201ca halfway decent GM wouldn't let those bad things happen anyway\u201d, true. But then, a halfway-decent GM can make lemonade out of lemons. That doesn't mean that the system desiers should feel content handing him lemons.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've lost me - where are these lemons that momentum is rectifying? What is it fixing that can't be addressed in the way I've said (on-the-fly by the GM)? I'm still not seeing what benefits it brings.<br /> <br /> Hrm. I'm going to go read this again tonight as I'm wondering if I've missed the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T16:31:58-07:00","id":540151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=540106#post540106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's put it this way: Sardonyx isn't so much \u201cfail forward\u201d as \u201cfail sideways\u201d: instead of the narrative stopping or even regressing, it twists.<br /> <br /> As for \u201ca halfway decent GM wouldn't let those bad things happen anyway\u201d, true. But then, a halfway-decent GM can make lemonade out of lemons. That doesn't mean that the system desiers should feel content handing him lemons.</div> </div> </div> </div>How Sardonyx works in practise remains to be seen! I am inclined to agree with you, however. When you fail, you don't regress, and you don't progress, but other options are opened, so failing sideways is a good description. A good GM maintains the illusion that the players could fail, thus keeping the stakes high, while actually ensuring that the story always progresses in whatever manner is best suited. Sardonyx doesn't seem to make the player's desired outcome inevitable, nor does it mean they cannot fail, but it might indeed allow the GM to facilitate those alternate possibilities through Momentum and the other thing I cannot recall the name of right now.<br /> <br /> So I remain positive! I hope that the system is not <i>too </i>cinematic in some ways, I want Aberrants to be able to just rinse baseline humans in contests where they are superhuman for example, rather than a baseline hero being able to defeat an Aberrant just because they are a hero. Winning just because you are a hero is crap and another reason why falling forward feels unsatisfying, though as noted, I don't think that Sardonyx really does that (happily enough!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T16:44:33-07:00","id":540164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=540124#post540124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I must be having very different gaming experiences - why would narrative stop or regress without a fail-forwards (or sideways) system?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You've lost me - where are these lemons that momentum is rectifying? What is it fixing that can't be addressed in the way I've said (on-the-fly by the GM)? I'm still not seeing what benefits it brings.<br /> <br /> Hrm. I'm going to go read this again tonight as I'm wondering if I've missed the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's put it this way, CHILL: for my first decade in roleplaying, my GM ran games <i>without any system whatsoever</i>. I'm <i>very</i> aware that a roleplaying system is at best of secondary importance to a competent GM, since a competent GM can make even the clunkiest system work and an incompetent GM will make a mess of even the most elegant system. So why have game systems at all? Why not instead devote all that page count to teaching GMs how to be competent? <br /> <br /> The answer that I've come up with for that is rather lengthy, and not what this topic is about; so I'll just mention that the best rules are the ones that highlight and encourage good GM practices. These rules concerning Momentum, Consolations, and Complications look like they do exactly that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T17:38:51-07:00","id":540206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=540164#post540164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's put it this way, CHILL: for my first decade in roleplaying, my GM ran games <i>without any system whatsoever</i>. I'm <i>very</i> aware that a roleplaying system is at best of secondary importance to a competent GM, since a competent GM can make even the clunkiest system work and an incompetent GM will make a mess of even the most elegant system. So why have game systems at all? Why not instead devote all that page count to teaching GMs how to be competent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, sure. But I'm not looking for and have not suggested systemless rules. I'm suggesting that <i>these specific rules as presented</i> seem cumbersome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=540164#post540164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answer that I've come up with for that is rather lengthy, and not what this topic is about; so I'll just mention that the best rules are the ones that highlight and encourage good GM practices. These rules concerning Momentum, Consolations, and Complications look like they do exactly that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, OK, I think we can agree that good rules can do that - but doesn't really shed any light on which 'lemons' you think are being addressed by these specifically. It seems you like how this is written and that's cool - It still feels to me like a solution looking for a problem so right now I'm unconvinced. <br /> <br /> But, yeah let's move on <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T18:58:50-07:00","id":540343,"title":"","content":"So we're moving on? Cool! Let's talk <i>powers.</i><br /> <br /> In principle, I loved the Aberrant freeform-ish superpower system -- more open than GURPS, more manageable than Champions. But as the saying goes: &quot;In theory, there's no difference between theory and practice. In practice, there is.&quot; I had to do a very careful juggling act STing Aberrant to avoid: a) a cakewalk for the PCs, and more importantly, b) one overpowered, um, power, making a fine red mist out of one. This was years before Mutants &amp; Masterminds (which I'd run Trinity in now if we weren't getting Sardonyx), so I just tap-danced as fast as I could. Since I love M&amp;M, that's my go-to baseline for powers now, but I'm curious to see what others think of rendering Daredevils, Psions, Novas, and Scions' super-ness in Sardonyx.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T20:43:20-07:00","id":540477,"title":"","content":"IMHO, there have been two major schools of superpower systems over the years; and ironically, they tend line up with the two major comic book companies. <br /> <br /> On the one hand, you have the DC class of RPGs, including but not limited to Mayfair Games' DC Heroes, Champions, GURPS Supers, and Mutants &amp; Masterminds. These games tend to favor a deconstructionist approach to powers, where they've dispassionately analyzed the assortment of powers out there and reduced them to a set of game effects and modifiers, complete with some sort of point-based power construction system. This leads to a robust game system capable of simulating a dizzying range of powers, but tends to encourage a gearhead mentality. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, you have the Marvel class of games, featuring the likes of Marvel Superheroes, Truth&amp;Justice, Marvel Heroic Adventure, and Icons. This tends toward a much more freeform approach to powers that doesn't try to spell out every little detail about what a given power can or can't do. Instead, it focuses on hitting the highlights and leaving the rest to the imagination of the player. Its main weakness lies in how much it depends on the GM and player being on the same page. <br /> <br /> Ironically, M&amp;M and Icons were created by the same guy (Steve Kenson). <br /> <br /> Aberrant 1e leaned toward the DC model. I'd like to see Aberrant 2e lean toward the Marvel model.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T20:54:41-07:00","id":540488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=539361#post539361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm seriously hoping not. To me those attributes complete and define the mental and social resistance perfectly. And when you are going to fight high appearance, high manipulation beings, those two attributes start to become essential.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to stress that I am not against the idea of Resistance stats for the Mental and Social categories. What I'm mostly opposed to is them being needlessly grey on when to use one or the other, or what the in-character difference is between the two.<br /> <br /> For instance, someone who has high Resolve could be said to be stubborn. Such a person should be difficult to persuade, and is under newer systems. The thing is though that it's not supposed to be the Social stat, it's the <i>Mental</i> stat. Likewise, things like perception are/were based around Composure, which is kinda weird - not nonsensical, but still kinda off - and notably, that doesn't really seem to be <i>social</i> in any real sense; you aren't really interacting with others. It makes it weird, because of the three social traits, it's the only one that operates when there is literally no one around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T21:14:23-07:00","id":540533,"title":"","content":"Really, I'd prefer to see Aberrant lean towards it's own model. I did like the game before for a reason. The main problem I tend to have with the DC model is that they tend to suck the flavor out of things in favor of increasingly more generic abilities, and that really makes powers unexciting after awhile. Aberrant had a good mix of powers that could be molded to whatever you wanted, along with powers that had a fairly predefined effect. It's good, because really I think outside of attack based powers, most powers aren't nearly so interchangeable as people make out.<br /> <br /> I would rather avoid too much focus on the power modifier model, where a character buys a base power and mods it out. Those can be flexible, but they tend to really slow down the character creation process and make these huge impenetrable stat blocks. Plus, nothing sucks like buying a power and then suddenly not having it work right because you forgot to buy the right modifier. I'd also add a personal preference note that I dislike how such systems tend to involve elements that seem too bound up in mechanical conceits and not in the game fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T21:57:42-07:00","id":540585,"title":"","content":"Yeah; that's more or less what I was trying to say. About the only point where we seem to disagree is that I see the 1e Aberrant model as leaning a bit too much in DC's direction. <br /> <br /> To clarify: <br /> \u2022 avoid systems that get so bound up in mechanical conceits that the game fiction gets lost in the mix.<br /> \u2022 avoid huge impenetrable stat blocks that try to pin down every little thing, such that if you overlook a modifier you don't get the power you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T00:03:45-07:00","id":540724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=540477#post540477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMHO, there have been two major schools of superpower systems over the years; and ironically, they tend line up with the two major comic book companies.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, you have the DC class of RPGs, including but not limited to Mayfair Games' DC Heroes, Champions, GURPS Supers, and Mutants &amp; Masterminds. These games tend to favor a deconstructionist approach to powers, where they've dispassionately analyzed the assortment of powers out there and reduced them to a set of game effects and modifiers, complete with some sort of point-based power construction system. This leads to a robust game system capable of simulating a dizzying range of powers, but tends to encourage a gearhead mentality.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you have the Marvel class of games, featuring the likes of Marvel Superheroes, Truth&amp;Justice, Marvel Heroic Adventure, and Icons. This tends toward a much more freeform approach to powers that doesn't try to spell out every little detail about what a given power can or can't do. Instead, it focuses on hitting the highlights and leaving the rest to the imagination of the player. Its main weakness lies in how much it depends on the GM and player being on the same page.<br /> <br /> Ironically, M&amp;M and Icons were created by the same guy (Steve Kenson).<br /> <br /> Aberrant 1e leaned toward the DC model. I'd like to see Aberrant 2e lean toward the Marvel model.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I would not. I dislike overly narrativist games and feel that Aberrant, being a game about having superpowers, should have proper, solid, interesting mechanics that really get into the grit of those superpowers. MHR roleplay is the opposite of what direction I would like from Aberrant, but Mutants and Masterminds trends too four colour for Aberrant as well (in the sense that in M&amp;M, double the power is only +1 to the rank).<br /> <br /> In Aberrant, if my character is several times as strong as the character he is fighting, or vice versa, then he rips their arms out. Doesn't matter what the narrative might suggest or that they both have super strength, that the hero deserves the win and we want to see the villain fall is nothing in the face of the harsh facts of superhuman combat. I hope that the Sardonyx system makes it clear that while you can punch above your weight, so to speak, actually chances are you'll just get wrecked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T07:51:38-07:00","id":541197,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I really appreciate the team making this preview available. Peeks behind the curtain are great for fans, but stressful for developers trying to balance getting feedback with saving some surprises.<br /> <br /> It's impossible to judge the entire system on just what's here, so here's my gut reactions to the parts we can see.<br /> <br /> <b>Enhancements. </b>This looks like a way to make actions more powerful, without altering their probability of success, like a poison that inflicts a bunch of damage but you\u2019ve got to scratch the target first. I like this and suspect I\u2019ll like it more when a list of examples is released.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Complication. </b>As an alternative to modifying the TN and/or dice pool to set difficulties, I think this mechanic will be faster and allow the players to inject more flavor into the actions. Thumbs up.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Consolation. </b>I really like this as a tool to make failures interesting, which has become a major goal in my personal GM\u2019ing skill set. I like the examples given, and I hope the full version of the text gives players the freedom to make suggestions.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Effect. </b>I\u2019m generally positive on this one. The examples that go along with this mechanic will be critical in establishing the power level of a \u2018point\u2019 of Effect.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Mixed Actions.</b> I\u2019m neutral on this. I\u2019d prefer a hard line of \u201cone action is one action,\u201d but if you\u2019re going to allow this sort of over-the-top-ness, this is a decent solution. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>When to Roll The Dice.</b> Excellent, in terms of rules, in terms of setting a tone of collaboration, and in terms of explicitly setting the precedent that players can negotiate.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Momentum</b> and the <b>Black Pool</b>. I think I see what the goal is -- not letting failures derail the game -- but it adds unnecessary complications. So I can\u2019t Activate a Power until someone fails? I\u2019m rolling a bunch of dice poorly in a Complex Attempt, and the solution to keep the action moving is to let me roll more dice? (Caveat: I don\u2019t find \u2018rolling lots of dice\u2019 to be particularly dramatic, so I\u2019m not a fan of the overall complex action.) With the Complications and Consolation mechanics already in play, I don't see the point of Momentum.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I do like the idea of<b> Immediate Aid</b>, so your failure helps your fellows, but I see that as a Consolation, not Momentum.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>The Red Pool. </b>Very much against. As part of Momentum, I don't see the utility. Additionally, as the GM, I have more than enough going on -- describing the world, responding to my 3 players destroying my prep work, balancing screen time, anticipating what comes next. Tracking an additional resource, one that may leave me unable to activate an NPC\u2019s dramatically appropriate ability? Nope. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Is the goal of the Red Pool to limit the GM\u2019s power? For my money, Sardonyx is going to be the base for a game that requires extraordinary GM trust from the players -- as a PC, your opponents could literally be gods. Attempting to put mechanical barriers in the GM\u2019s path seems counter-intuitive.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","user":"PaulChapman","date":". 06-05-2015, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T08:01:08-07:00","id":541211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=540029#post540029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *twitch* Don't take this the wrong way, but I have a real issue with this sentiment. I look for a good experience in games, not to win. Some of the best gaming experiences I've seen around the table come from completely and utter failure - especially from unfavorable dice rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I have had some really memorable moments in my games that stemmed from failures, as well. However, they were not PLANNED! I did not PLAN on losing that dice roll. It just happened and led to some great stories. When I pick up the dice, I expect to win that roll. I expect to come out on top. I expect to hit my target number/difficulty. I expect to cause a lot of damage in my hit. That is my point. <br /> <br /> With the new system, I do not care whether I would win or lose the roll of the dice. I will always get something. It may not be readily apparent. It may not be what I wanted...but when I pick up the dice, I do not care if I hit the mark or not. That is what I am digging about it. <br /> <br /> As far as the power models go, I kind of lean towards &quot;Give me the basics, I can do the rest from there.&quot; I like a game like Champions that says &quot;You have the ability to cause damage at a distance.&quot; and then I choose if it is electricity or fire or gamma radiation blasts or shooting my fingernails. I then get to take the base of &quot;I do x amount of damage out to a range of y meters.&quot; and then I customize it. It allows me to make my character's powers and make them my own. <br /> <br /> It is always something that I like to do: make my character my own. I do it from the concept and I will do it with the attributes and abilities and merits and backgrounds. Since the powers are going to be a part of the character, I want to customize those as well. Please understand that I am not talking about being a &quot;special snowflake&quot; but just make him something that screams &quot;The Donnie.&quot;<br /> <br /> However, I am really excited about the rules since they seem to have even done that with the dice mechanics. Rather than go &quot;X amount of successes means ____ happens.&quot; it is now &quot;So you have X amount of successes. What do YOU want to do with them?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T09:55:20-07:00","id":541376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=541211#post541211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the new system, I do not care whether I would win or lose the roll of the dice. I will always get something. It may not be readily apparent. It may not be what I wanted...but when I pick up the dice, I do not care if I hit the mark or not. That is what I am digging about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I can see that - if that's what you want. The concept just doesn't do it for me. But then I've never really cared if I win or lose a dice roll. I don't believe you should always expect to get something on a dice roll. Some you 'win', some you 'lose' and that's absolutely, perfectly fine to me. As a player I think part of the fun is roleplaying your way around and through (often as a result of roll-of-the-dice) failures. Then again I don't think of this in terms of winning or losing and don't need mechanics level incentives to actually 'act' in game - which appears to be what this is trying to 'fix (see my comments earlier that this feels like a solution in search of a problem).<br /> <br /> But, I can see that if the approach is to make this more of a pulp-hero system where the 'good guys' always come through, then it might work (but I'm still concerned it'll be cumbersome). However, I find that all pulp-hero stuff terribly predictable and not very interesting, frankly, so that's probably influencing my view on this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T10:46:48-07:00","id":541445,"title":"","content":"Having been part of many games in which a failure immediately put the plot to a halt, and a couple others in which the distinction between failure and successes was nearly existent because the story moved forward in basically the same manner either way, I'm glad for Consolations being an explicit part of the system and consider it a solution for a clearly already found problem.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile black/red momentum doesn't strike me as hard to keep track off, and provides an avenue for the kind of dramatic, cinematic swings I have been wanting in games in recent years, so I'm glad for it too.<br /> <br /> As for powers, well, I'm an M&amp;M guy, so I'm in favor of leaning in that direction, much like it did in the previous system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T10:48:46-07:00","id":541447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=541197#post541197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Momentum</b> and the <b>Black Pool</b>. I think I see what the goal is -- not letting failures derail the game -- but it adds unnecessary complications. So I can\u2019t Activate a Power until someone fails? I\u2019m rolling a bunch of dice poorly in a Complex Attempt, and the solution to keep the action moving is to let me roll more dice? (Caveat: I don\u2019t find \u2018rolling lots of dice\u2019 to be particularly dramatic, so I\u2019m not a fan of the overall complex action.) With the Complications and Consolation mechanics already in play, I don't see the point of Momentum.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>It's really more about mechanizing the Gambler's Fallacy and creating a sense of dramatic tension leading to a climax.<br /> <br /> This is important: activating a power isn't something done <i>solely</i> with Momentum, but we left the option so system writers can use it as something you can spend Momentum on. They might do that - they might make powers per-encounter or per-session or whatever. When you see timing rules and initiative, you'll see that we broke up the game like a multiple-season television show, complete with episodes (and smaller scenes within those episodes). For all I know, a future Sardoynx game might make powers something you can only spend at certain points of the episode, I dunno. We wanted to keep the option open, is all I'm saying - but powers may, or may not, cost Momentum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>The Red Pool. </b>Very much against. As part of Momentum, I don't see the utility. Additionally, as the GM, I have more than enough going on -- describing the world, responding to my 3 players destroying my prep work, balancing screen time, anticipating what comes next. Tracking an additional resource, one that may leave me unable to activate an NPC\u2019s dramatically appropriate ability? Nope. </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Well, there probably won't be that many resources - in fact, in Mundane level play, there may <i>only </i>be Momentum. It's only the higher Tiers that have an additional fuel trait.<br /> <br /> It may help that there's no Willpower in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Is the goal of the Red Pool to limit the GM\u2019s power? For my money, Sardonyx is going to be the base for a game that requires extraordinary GM trust from the players -- as a PC, your opponents could literally be gods. Attempting to put mechanical barriers in the GM\u2019s path seems counter-intuitive.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>No, that's not it at all! The Red Pool is both a variant of Momentum for the NPCs to use, but the GM can also use it to indirectly aid the PCs (by boosting friendly NPCs). It's something to increase the power of the GM, not limit it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T11:52:22-07:00","id":541529,"title":"","content":"It does seem like the system very much wants to resolve stuff quickly (good!) but with a wide variation of granularity (extra good!).<br /> <br /> The risk of having too many variable resources to track is very much a real thing, but I think that the removal of classic WW-isms like Willpower and such will help with that. So far, it seems very much like a clean system which is narrativist enough to be dramatic but simulationist enough to actually be somewhat realistic and engaging, which is good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T13:31:51-07:00","id":541637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=541447#post541447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really more about mechanizing the Gambler's Fallacy and creating a sense of dramatic tension leading to a climax.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a mechanical expression of Gambler's Fallacy, it's a good one. However, I need some help seeing how this mechanic will lead to &quot;a sense of dramatic tension leading to a climax.&quot;<br /> <br /> How would Momentum apply to, say, Die Hard? The anime Bleach? Kill Bill? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=541447#post541447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is important: activating a power isn't something done <i>solely</i> with Momentum, but we left the option so system writers can use it as something you can spend Momentum on. They might do that - they might make powers per-encounter or per-session or whatever. When you see timing rules and initiative, you'll see that we broke up the game like a multiple-season television show, complete with episodes (and smaller scenes within those episodes). For all I know, a future Sardoynx game might make powers something you can only spend at certain points of the episode, I dunno. We wanted to keep the option open, is all I'm saying - but powers may, or may not, cost Momentum.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Activate a Power is a placeholder. I really should have realized that, considering it says it in the description. Leaping then looking.<br /> <br /> Immediate Aid is actually a Consolation; not sure why it's listed in the Momentum section.<br /> <br /> Focus Action relies on the undefined &quot;Focus&quot; so I ignored it previously, but if it allows one player to snag all the accumulated Momentum, that seems kinda cruddy -- spotlight hogs are going to love it, to the detriment of the rest of the table. Unless there's going to be lots more than 12-15 dice in that pool . . . in which case, we're going to need a bigger bowl.<br /> <br /> Complex Attempt gets a solid &quot;meh&quot; due to being linked to a mechanic I don't care for.<br /> <br /> Which is all a long way of saying: I don't really see how Momentum is going to work in play. I see a pool that gets filled when PCs roll poorly, but don't see how said pool positively effects the flow of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=541447#post541447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there probably won't be that many resources - in fact, in Mundane level play, there may <i>only </i>be Momentum. It's only the higher Tiers that have an additional fuel trait.<br /> <br /> It may help that there's no Willpower in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as the Director is managing a number of NPCs, there's plenty of resources to keep track of: attributes and attitudes, health and motivations, cash and ammo. Know my biggest problem with the Inspiration system in D&amp;D is? Remembering to award it. I have the same trouble in Fate Core, but at least that system puts the fate point flow in my face constantly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=541447#post541447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that's not it at all! The Red Pool is both a variant of Momentum for the NPCs to use, but the GM can also use it to indirectly aid the PCs (by boosting friendly NPCs). It's something to increase the power of the GM, not limit it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, without knowing how Momentum effects the game, I can't really evaluate that statement. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, just based on the document released so far, I'd expect to boost friendly NPCs by providing Effects.<br /> <br /> Ah, the fun of extrapolating an entire RPG from a single small chunk of mechanics. Aren't fans great? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T13:57:01-07:00","id":541659,"title":"","content":"Immediate Aid is <i>not</i> a Consolation; it's &quot;Angela generates a point of Momentum; Bart spends it.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for remembering to award Momentum: there might be other ways of earning Momentum that require the Director to remember to award them (much like various Storyteller/ing games occasionally require the Storyteller to remember to hand out Willpower); but this isn't one of them: \u201cyou just failed a roll; add a point of Momentum\u201d is the sort of thing that's likely to become <i>automatic</i> after a cery short time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T15:28:13-07:00","id":541761,"title":"","content":"Die Hard? John McClane gets the tar beaten out of him and acquires Momentum (such as when the blond guy kicks the crap out of him). John's player seems to really like to risk getting killed until s/he maxes out the black pool. That floor covered in glass is a hell of a Complication.<br /> <br /> Kill Bill? The Bride built a maxed out black pool before going into a coma. After that she mostly wins because she's almost certainly a Daredevil, so Momentum isn't much of an issue, though Acceleration may be in play. I suspect there's some serious Daredevil-age going on.<br /> <br /> I don't know Bleach well.<br /> <br /> Yeah, power activation is an option listed in the document for line designers to use or not. Same with options like Acceleration.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T15:42:14-07:00","id":541771,"title":"","content":"What's Acceleration (acceleration)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T16:25:19-07:00","id":541797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=541761#post541761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know Bleach well.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Ichigo got the shit beat out of him without being able to fight back in any significant manner =&gt; Ichigo effortlessly crushes whoever just pummeled him into a fine paste&quot; is a recurring theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":54,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","user":"Tiresias","date":". 06-05-2015, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T16:52:28-07:00","id":541840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=541771#post541771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's Acceleration (acceleration)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Acceleration is an optional rule for Momentum during high action scenes in which the Black and Red pools each gain increasing amounts of Momentum (capping out at +5 a turn). I assume the point is to encourage players to spend Momentum like crazy because their maximum cap applies so if they're not using Momentum it's just wasted while the Red pool will keep growing.<br /> <br /> It's basically a reason to cut loose with Momentum because it will start flowing like mad rather than trying to build it up over a bunch of actions until it's high enough to be worth using on a big roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T17:00:15-07:00","id":541845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=541659#post541659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Immediate Aid is <i>not</i> a Consolation; it's &quot;Angela generates a point of Momentum; Bart spends it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Compare Immediate Aid to Minor Enhancement. They function identically, except one is for the failing player, and the other is shared with another character. It can't be banked (like Momentum), and are as &quot;real&quot; to the in-game fiction as Minor Enhancement (unlike Momentum, which is described as &quot;purely a game construct to shape the fiction).<br /> <br /> IMO, if it quacks like a duck . . . As more details on Consolation and Momentum are released, the divide may become more sharp, and the placement of IA into Momentum may become obvious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=541659#post541659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for remembering to award Momentum: there might be other ways of earning Momentum that require the Director to remember to award them (much like various Storyteller/ing games occasionally require the Storyteller to remember to hand out Willpower); but this isn't one of them: \u201cyou just failed a roll; add a point of Momentum\u201d is the sort of thing that's likely to become <i>automatic</i> after a cery short time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rereading my post, I see why you may think I was concerned with remembering to award Momentum. However, my actual concern is that it's just one more &quot;thing&quot; -- like the NPC's health level or motivations, or the phase of the moon, or a thousand other details the Director is responsible for -- for me to keep track of. <br /> <br /> I prefer lighter, more streamlined systems these days.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T17:04:54-07:00","id":541847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=541761#post541761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Die Hard? John McClane gets the tar beaten out of him and acquires Momentum (such as when the blond guy kicks the crap out of him). John's player seems to really like to risk getting killed until s/he maxes out the black pool. That floor covered in glass is a hell of a Complication.<br /> <br /> Kill Bill? The Bride built a maxed out black pool before going into a coma. After that she mostly wins because she's almost certainly a Daredevil, so Momentum isn't much of an issue, though Acceleration may be in play. I suspect there's some serious Daredevil-age going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Malcolm, but I'm pretty clear on how dice get added to the Momentum pool; what I'm not seeing is how they're used. Of the four spends listed, I don't see how they're applied to these films. Neither the Bride nor McClane had anyone to Immediate Aid, they didn't seem to be doing any Complex Attempts, and there didn't seem to be any Powers Activated. I suppose they could be Focused?<br /> <br /> Thanks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T21:06:24-07:00","id":542093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=541847#post541847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks Malcolm, but I'm pretty clear on how dice get added to the Momentum pool; what I'm not seeing is how they're used. Of the four spends listed, I don't see how they're applied to these films. Neither the Bride nor McClane had anyone to Immediate Aid, they didn't seem to be doing any Complex Attempts, and there didn't seem to be any Powers Activated. I suppose they could be Focused?<br /> <br /> Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Focus Action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T21:27:05-07:00","id":542108,"title":"","content":"These kind of things are pretty easy to track when you have physical tokens though, which sounds like the intent.<br /> <br /> The red pool sounds like a necessity for NPCs if Willpower is not a thing.<br /> <br /> Technically, Momentum really just appears to be a form on Consolation, since if you either gain Momentum or spend it immediately on others, you don't get any other Consolation. The biggest difference between Minor Enhancement and Immediate Aid seems to be choice; the Director chooses your Consolation, and if she says a Minor Enhancement isn't available, then it isn't available. Conversely the players seem to be the one to choose whether to bank gained Momentum or spend it on Immediate Aid. Likewise, a player can choose Momentum over a Consolation if they wish, but not the reverse. That's likely why Immediate Aid isn't classified as a Consolation, because it is always on the table for a failed roll-you can always pick to use it on a failure-while things normally classed as Consolations aren't.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's a matter of always &quot;winning&quot; on rolls so much as it tries to make failed rolls more meaningful and interesting. It doesn't mean you can't fuck up, just that when you do you still have somewhere to go. It also means you are having some kind of impact besides just finishing another bag Cheetos.<br /> <br /> I like the teamwork dynamic of Immediate Aid, I really do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T21:31:28-07:00","id":542128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=540724#post540724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I would not. I dislike overly narrativist games and feel that Aberrant, being a game about having superpowers, should have proper, solid, interesting mechanics that really get into the grit of those superpowers. MHR roleplay is the opposite of what direction I would like from Aberrant, but Mutants and Masterminds trends too four colour for Aberrant as well (in the sense that in M&amp;M, double the power is only +1 to the rank).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would keep in mind we are working on a gradient here,; we don't have to choose between Hero System and entirely freeform. I prefer some solid underlying mechanics myself, but those mechanics need to be easy to use, compact, and flavorful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T21:39:19-07:00","id":542190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=542093#post542093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Focus Action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of the focus action, the text says you can't spend less than your character maximum. What if there are not that many dice in the pool? Are you unable to use Focus Action, or does it just use all the dice in the pool?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T22:26:37-07:00","id":542262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=542190#post542190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of the focus action, the text says you can't spend less than your character maximum. What if there are not that many dice in the pool? Are you unable to use Focus Action, or does it just use all the dice in the pool?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, you use all the dice that happen to be there. This entails something of a strategic mindset. Do you zero the pool now, or wait until it hits its peak, risking further harm and failure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T01:52:07-07:00","id":542390,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>My impression on the Sardonyx system</b></span> (based on the teaser)<br /> <br /> <b>About me:</b> I was a big fan of Vampire the Masquerade, though I had the usual gripes with the rules: the chance of botching actually increasing with your skill, three different ways to alter difficulty, four rolls to resolve an attack not counting the constant rerolls for \u201c0\u201ds and 1s deducting from successes. Ah \u2013 and beauty (appearance) as an attribute wasn\u2019t a smart move either. The rules were a mess, but could easily be houseruled. The Revised Storyteller system for the Trinity games almost completely repaired all problems I had with the rules. nWoD I found too abstract, though mirrors had good solutions for that. The new nWoD (God Machine Chronicles) lost me completely. Too meta gamey, too reliant on Willpower, too complicated conditions. And again: much too meta gamey. That\u2019s my history with the Storyteller / Storytelling rules.<br /> <br /> Now to Sardonyx<br /> <br /> <u><b>Part I: the die rolls</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Difficulty is the number of successes you need to overcome.</b> I just love what you did here. For the first time, you really have only one difficulty mechanism (we\u2019ll talk about Momentum later), and it is the right one. It is very similar to the Revised Storyteller rules, but much stricter. By <b>keeping the number of dice and the target number fixed</b>, the players have very little to consider. As a GM you can just say \u201croll shooting\u201d or \u201croll dex + firearms\u201d. This is great. Keep it that way!<br /> <br /> <b>\u201c0\u201d count as two successes.</b> Just like in the first Exalted rules version. I just love that! This prevents the time stealing and unnecessary constant rerolling and makes the game more streamlined and much faster, though rerolling sometimes raised the suspense and freak-rolls with small dice pools from time to time were fun. Still: the best possible solution. Two thumbs up (three if you are a mutant).<br /> <br /> <b>Conclusion: </b>I love what you did to the basic mechanisms. I am thrilled. Now I\u2019ll wait for the rules for damage, armor, soaking, dodging, etc. to tell, if combat will live up to this streamlining.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Part II: Effects</b></u><br /> <br /> I am not sure about this. On the one hand, I love being given options. On the other hand, this may slow down the game considerably. Ever played Dragon Age? You ponder on how to spend your stunt points constantly. Sometimes this is fun, sometimes this is a drag, sometimes it is a curse because you have trouble trying to call for a maneuver as you don\u2019t know if you\u2019ll have the stunt points necessary. This reminds me of that. My impression: offer not more than one or two options for the game and maybe one (and only one) special option for each power.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Part III: Consolation and Momentum</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>I hate meta gaming forced by the rules.</b> I just can\u2019t stand it. One of the reasons I am playing the good old Revised Storytelling games is, that the narrative part comes along without rules from the players and the GM just naturally. Being forced to come up with a special narrative, dictated by the rules, is something, that I don\u2019t want to see in this game. If I want that kind of gameplay, I\u2019ll play Dungeon World or Apocalypse World or one of those World-Games. But I don\u2019t. Problem is: they are so successful, that now every game feels compelled to be more narrative driven. My wish: don\u2019t make such a game!<br /> <br /> <b>Consolation</b> just is a meta gamey thing that can be left out with just the advice \u201cdon\u2019t let a bad die role get in the way of the adventure\u201d. There: now you don\u2019t need consolation anymore. Just leave it out. Nobody really needs it.<br /> <br /> <b>Momentum</b>: a resource that is fueled by failures is not a bad idea. <b>Momentum</b> might be some genius move. But again: not too much meta game, please. As a player I want to immerse in the character, want to live through the story, not design it. I want failures to feel as failures and not as another meaningless way to get along. So I would not give Momentum for a \u201cGame Master fiat\u201d, as this would make a \u201cGame Master fiat\u201d a) all the more popular (you got Momentum for it, so why do you complain) and b) make it obvious.<br /> <br /> I feel having one pool for the whole party is a bad idea. I know my gaming group and I know what would happen. Everybody would try to pay into that pool and everybody would be reluctant to draw from it. I\u2019d rather give everybody a personal pool.<br /> <br /> <b>What I like about momentum: </b>spending it isn\u2019t meta gamey at all. It is all a mechanic that doesn\u2019t change the story but lets you succeed more often or might fuel powers. This is cool.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Part IV: summary</b></u><br /> <br /> I love that you built up a really stable and fast core mechanic, though I\u2019ll have to wait for the complete combat rules to judge. I just love what I can see here. On the other hand I got the impression, that you want to make a more story driven game and much more meta gamy kind of playstyle. I don\u2019t like that at all. As long as I can ignore these narrative parts easily I don\u2019t care. But I am not sure about that.<br /> <br /> All of my evaluation is on purely personal basis. Other people might long for more meta gaming, more story driven games. Still \u2013 I\u2019d like to see the new rules set be a better version of the older rules, not a complete change of the gaming paradigm from gam/sim to nar. But that is just me.<br /> <br /> This was a long post. You all earned a point of Momentum ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1138-dailor","user":"dailor","date":". 06-06-2015, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1138-dailor","name":"dailor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T22:53:55-07:00","id":543478,"title":"","content":"See, I think the meta elements of the game are very, very important, as the main two genres the system is primarily there to emulate (Super/pulp hero and Mythology) are as much about the art of storytelling as the actual story itself. Without a heavily metafictional bent to the system I feel that something close to the heart of the genres is lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T03:17:22-07:00","id":543680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=543478#post543478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I think the meta elements of the game are very, very important, as the main two genres the system is primarily there to emulate (Super/pulp hero and Mythology) are as much about the art of storytelling as the actual story itself. Without a heavily metafictional bent to the system I feel that something close to the heart of the genres is lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure, if we are on the same page about metagaming and narrative elements. Meta gaming means: you think about the mechanics or the story as a whole, not in-character. My primarys reason to roleplay is immersion, so metagaming is the opposite of that. Building up a good story while being immersed was perfectly possible with the revised storyteller rules. I see nothing gained by consolation whatsoever. Consolation tries to repair, what wasn't broken in my book. If you have your focus on narrating, then consolation is perfect for you. But I don't think, this has anything to do with the setting/genre, because they worked perfectly for me without being forced and limited to certain narratives by rules.<br /> <br /> What exactly is it, that makes - in your opinion - thinking about about the development of the story out of the possibilities of your character and forcing certain narratives by rules so essential for these settings? And why wasn't it necessary with the old rules set?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1138-dailor","name":"dailor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T08:29:22-07:00","id":543910,"title":"","content":"My primary reason to play role-playing games is to experience the duality of a mechanical game combined with imaginative creation. Pure immersion would be better simply free-forming everything.<br /> <br /> Consolations try to fix what is broken, that is, when you fail a roll and the story comes to a dead stop. No, you don't need a explicit mechanical fix for this, but by putting it in the rules directly, at the core, we redefine what failure means in the setting so it's readily obvious what that solution is rather than having it be some supah-secret thing that the GM is only supposed to figure out on their own after 10+ years of play.<br /> <br /> I would also say it's not very limited. Yes, there are only four categories. Those categories are very broad. Extra information and social benefit could be damn near anything.<br /> <br /> You are also <i>not required to give Consolations</i>. If you don't like them, or they don't make sense in the context of what's going on, then you don't give them out and the players just get Momentum instead.<br /> <br /> Instead of thinking of Consolations as their own category of things, think about them as what they are, which is an alternative to Momentum. If a player fails and you want to give them something so everything doesn't come to a screeching halt, it wouldn't be fair for them to gain that AND Momentum. Consolations make results more fair and give players an interesting choice.<br /> <br /> I'm really getting sick of trying to remember how to spell Consolations, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T09:17:44-07:00","id":543942,"title":"","content":"Hey. Designer here. I hear you about not wanting there to be narrative interference that's too strident. I want the world to have integrity. That means Momentum has specific limitations to make sure it satisfies its function, which is really to prevent long strings of blown rolls derailing play. I designed Momentum because many narrative systems that say they fix this actually make it worse, or makes failure completely meaningless. It's funny that you mention Consolation, because it's really the part of the system that serves as &quot;training wheels&quot; for people used to heavy narrative fail-forward systems, who may be afraid to take a chance with Momentum. <br /> <br /> I'm not so interested in imposing larger structural narratives, but supporting up and down beats. &quot;Fail forward&quot; mechanics often hand out little crumbs of satisfaction, that make success feel less satisfying, and the general rhythm of a game feel flat. You do have a &quot;crumb&quot; option, but you also have the &quot;no cake, no cake, no cake EAT THE DAMN CAKE&quot; flow, which is more dramatic and also introduces the possibility that you might wait too long and go down in flames. I want you to get cool variations in play *and* stay connected to the world on its own terms, but I submit a two game losing streak is just as game-breaking as arbitrary success because of &quot;story needs.&quot; Consolation and Momentum are ultimately about flow, not big structure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T13:33:35-07:00","id":544216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=543910#post543910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consolations try to fix what is broken, that is, when you fail a roll and the story comes to a dead stop. No, you don't need a explicit mechanical fix for this, but by putting it in the rules directly, at the core, we redefine what failure means in the setting so it's readily obvious what that solution is rather than having it be some supah-secret thing that the GM is only supposed to figure out on their own after 10+ years of play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still not buying some of this to be honest.<br /> <br /> I think failure is an entirely reasonable option personally and have no need of incentives or rewards when 'failing', so let's not assume failure is always a bad thing that needs fixing (seriously, when did that become a thing?).<br /> <br /> That said, if these considerations (and I'm counting Momentum here too), were entirely optional at a system level then fair enough, I could see that as maybe useful to those who need it. What I'd prefer is some well-written guidance for newer players and GM's helping them understand how they can run better story-driven games through good judgement / decision making, and ditch trying to write rules for that process. What's wrong with some solid well written advice on many ways to tackle such situations instead of a bunch of rules mechanics?<br /> <br /> I can see Malcolm's underlying reasoning, but whereas before I had a hunch this was a solution looking for a problem, now I'm convinced it is. I have never seen this problem in a game (from Malcolms post above):<br /> <br /> &quot;That means Momentum has specific limitations to make sure it satisfies its function, <i><b>which is really to prevent long strings of blown rolls derailing pla</b></i>y&quot;<br /> <br /> After multiple readings I find myself still hoping its going to be relatively easy, without a time consuming rewrite, to ignore these parts of the system. I can see ignoring Consolations as relatively straightforward based on what Malcolm said above, but I'm concerned Momentum is too important to the wider system(s) to easily ignore it without major follow-on issues.<br /> <br /> Does anyone know if there is any option planned for Momentum-less play at a mechanics level or something far more streamlined as an alternative?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":232,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","user":"CHILL","date":". 06-07-2015, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T14:10:08-07:00","id":544243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=544216#post544216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think failure is an entirely reasonable option personally and have no need of incentives or rewards when 'failing', so let's not assume failure is always a bad thing that needs fixing (seriously, when did that become a thing?).</div> </div> </div> </div>This feels like a really long in-grained rule zero fallacy.<br /> <br /> Failures at key moments (or strings of failures) getting in the way has <b>always</b> been a thing. The issue is that it's been a think for so long, most of us have internalized ways to get around it. It's very hard for me to see any stance where this shouldn't be addressed as a problem to fix, that isn't just dropping off, &quot;because I already fix it in my head.&quot;<br /> <br /> Any time the mechanics have a potential to get in the way of the fun the game is trying to encourage, it's a problem. Giving game based tools to fix it is a solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T15:56:59-07:00","id":544356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=543942#post543942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey. Designer here. I hear you about not wanting there to be narrative interference that's too strident. I want the world to have integrity. That means Momentum has specific limitations to make sure it satisfies its function, which is really to prevent long strings of blown rolls derailing play. I designed Momentum because many narrative systems that say they fix this actually make it worse, or makes failure completely meaningless. It's funny that you mention Consolation, because it's really the part of the system that serves as &quot;training wheels&quot; for people used to heavy narrative fail-forward systems, who may be afraid to take a chance with Momentum.<br /> <br /> I'm not so interested in imposing larger structural narratives, but supporting up and down beats. &quot;Fail forward&quot; mechanics often hand out little crumbs of satisfaction, that make success feel less satisfying, and the general rhythm of a game feel flat. You do have a &quot;crumb&quot; option, but you also have the &quot;no cake, no cake, no cake EAT THE DAMN CAKE&quot; flow, which is more dramatic and also introduces the possibility that you might wait too long and go down in flames. I want you to get cool variations in play *and* stay connected to the world on its own terms, but I submit a two game losing streak is just as game-breaking as arbitrary success because of &quot;story needs.&quot; Consolation and Momentum are ultimately about flow, not big structure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly I don't like to constantly &quot;retcon&quot; the narrative to include different options should players fail, because I like to present them with information and let them plan things out themselves. Consolations will therefore be somewhat rare seredipities that come up naturally in play as a result of the existing scenario set-up (&quot;you miss the guy with your gunfire, but hit the plate window behind him and shower him with shards of broken glass&quot; is not retconning anything, it's just providing a mechanical outcome which comes naturally from not hitting the guy, and hitting the window instead. If the player wants, they can take the momentum, and the glass blows out the other way, or the bullets just through and through). Mostly I'll just let the Momentum pool build, I imagine.<br /> <br /> Seems like a different system from what I usually like, but also quite positive in many ways. Fall Forward Narrativist games are often mechnically boring to me and this doesn't seem boring so that's definitely a plus!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T17:15:45-07:00","id":544506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=544243#post544243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The issue is that it's been a think for so long, most of us have internalized ways to get around it. It's very hard for me to see any stance where this shouldn't be addressed as a problem to fix, that isn't just dropping off, &quot;because I already fix it in my head.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if that's true for all groups / GM's (which I don't agree with just from my own experience), I'm still not convinced that more dice / mechanics is the way to go for every time a dice roll doesn't come out in a character's favor - and I actively dislike when those mechanics require tracking one or more pools which can subsequently be spent on x, y or z options. Personal preference and all that. As a GM I prefer things like combat to be streamlined with little admin.<br /> <br /> As I've said, hopefully there's some way to make the concept of Momentum optional, or at the least a couple different (more streamlined) options for how the system handles fail-sideways / fail-forwards or whatever we're calling it if we have to have a system level process for it. Definitely something without pools to track and points to spend on effects. A simple bonus here or there, optionally, perhaps.<br /> <br /> I am really liking plenty of the other components of the system though such as how difficulty, target numbers and so on are handled. While only personally interested in the Aeon setting, I can see how tiered play will be a great way to handle scale in a setting like Aberrant - that'll be interesting to read more about. Hearing that Willpower has possibly been removed is very welcome news. There's a running joke with one group I've gamed with since the Vampire 1st came out that 'Willpower is just for looking at&quot;. So yeah, no loss there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T17:41:31-07:00","id":544570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=544243#post544243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This feels like a really long in-grained rule zero fallacy.<br /> <br /> Failures at key moments (or strings of failures) getting in the way has <b>always</b> been a thing. The issue is that it's been a think for so long, most of us have internalized ways to get around it. It's very hard for me to see any stance where this shouldn't be addressed as a problem to fix, that isn't just dropping off, &quot;because I already fix it in my head.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a great way to put it and Took me years to 1) notice I was doing it, and 2) break myself of doing it subconsciously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T19:41:10-07:00","id":544653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=544216#post544216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still not buying some of this to be honest.<br /> <br /> I think failure is an entirely reasonable option personally and have no need of incentives or rewards when 'failing', so let's not assume failure is always a bad thing that needs fixing (seriously, when did that become a thing?).</div> </div> </div> </div>You are conflating all failure with game-breaking failure, and setting up a straw man. Game-breaking failure is when you have failure that just kills all momentum, small m. This is a problem that was brought up numerous times in Call of Cthulhu over the years - players would go to investigate something, blow their roll, and be unable to make any progress in the scenario because of it, and a whole new game was developed specifically to deal with that problem.<br /> <br /> You can still very much fail, and failure is still a bad thing - if I fail to catch my daughter when Dr. Violence chucks her off a skyscraper, she's still dead, and I have to live with that. Now maybe someone sees my daughter get brutally killed in front of me and offers me sympathy. Maybe I just get a bonus to my roll to punch him in the face later. Maybe, just maybe, I get some other second shot at saving her, but the Consolation isn't going to save her for me, even if offered.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T20:10:20-07:00","id":544686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=544653#post544653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are conflating all failure with game-breaking failure, and setting up a straw man. Game-breaking failure is when you have failure that just kills all momentum, small m.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how you're reaching that conclusion from what I've said so far. Momentum does not, as written, appear to address something we're calling 'game breaking failure' in this thread. In the released document it specifically states:<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">On her character\u2019s failure, a player may either add 1 point of Momentum to the black pool (see below) or \u201cspend\u201d it immediately by giving another player\u2019s character a 1 success&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">That reads to me that its on every dice roll that fails. You fail, you fire up the Momentum mechanic. Sure, this is a preview and playtesting will be key to se how it shakes out as I've said before. I think the concept of using momentum as a result of failing on a dice roll is overkill. I'd prefer a way to avoid using that component completely. Make it optional and I'm good.<br /> <br /> Oh, and quickly for the Cthulhu example (and this works for any 'but the rules break!' examples) - what I think is useful is advice for the GM on how to handle crappy systems / how to roleplay when things don't go to plan, not </span><i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">even more system mechanics.</span> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i></span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T21:30:11-07:00","id":544764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=544506#post544506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if that's true for all groups / GM's (which I don't agree with just from my own experience), I'm still not convinced that more dice / mechanics is the way to go for every time a dice roll doesn't come out in a character's favor - and I actively dislike when those mechanics require tracking one or more pools which can subsequently be spent on x, y or z options. Personal preference and all that. As a GM I prefer things like combat to be streamlined with little admin.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with your stance is that it lets you criticize things based on your preference and dress it up as more.<br /> <br /> Since free-form RP is a thing that actually works and is fun (not for everyone of course, but people clearly enjoy it), we can make the case that <i>any rule</i> is the wrong way to go over just giving better GM advice.<br /> <br /> Rules and mechanics are there to facilitate the game because we generally agree that they add to the experience. More mechanics that serve the game's goals are better than a lack of rules and some text about how to handle not having rules for what the game says is supposed to happen. Mechanics need to be judged in their context. &quot;I don't like more mechanics&quot; is an inherently unusable metric.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure how you're reaching that conclusion from what I've said so far. Momentum does not, as written, appear to address something we're calling 'game breaking failure' in this thread. In the released document it specifically states: </div> </div> </div>It gives the players a metacurrency to help avoid them. When something big comes up, they have Momentum from any failures from things not going well to make a big roll and move things forward.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That reads to me that its on every dice roll that fails. You fail, you fire up the Momentum mechanic. Sure, this is a preview and playtesting will be key to se how it shakes out as I've said before. I think the concept of using momentum as a result of failing on a dice roll is overkill. I'd prefer a way to avoid using that component completely. Make it optional and I'm good.<br /> <br /> Oh, and quickly for the Cthulhu example (and this works for any 'but the rules break!' examples) - what I think is useful is advice for the GM on how to handle crappy systems / how to roleplay when things don't go to plan, not <i>even more system mechanics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i> </div> </div> </div>Yes, when you fail you drop a counter into the black pool if you don't get/opt for a consolation, and one of the main uses is to spend it before it goes in (so even then it isn't every time).<br /> <br /> The problem is you're basically just going around in circles regarding &quot;overkill.&quot; Failures generate momentum, which can be used to offset future failures. You can't really show its overkill without relying on your own premise (more = bad) to get to your conclusion.<br /> <br /> As well, you're not really showing why GM advice and mechanics are even at odds with each other here. You're even acknowledging that the rules do break, but saying, &quot;GMs should just fix it, not the rules.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T06:26:20-07:00","id":545107,"title":"","content":"Ultimately we want failure to have consequences and support rising tension by encouraging people to wait for success. Further playtesting will determine how the rubber hits the road here. I can't really speak for suggestions to freeform or wing it except to note that you can always do that--but the problems we approach through game design assume the game is the medium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T06:38:23-07:00","id":545117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=544764#post544764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well, you're not really showing why GM advice and mechanics are even at odds with each other here. You're even acknowledging that the rules do break, but saying, &quot;GMs should just fix it, not the rules.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying more rules do not necessarily = good, and in this specific case I feel the rules presented add unnecessary admin to a process which I feel should flow much more smoothly. That doesn't inherently mean I prefer no rules, or that rules don't break. I'm saying these specific components of the new system don't work well as written. I'm also far from the only one with reservations about them, so let's stop suggesting I'm somehow just not seeing the light here and my viewpoint is skewed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Its a difference in playing styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T08:33:52-07:00","id":545337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=545107#post545107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately we want failure to have consequences and support rising tension by encouraging people to wait for success.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I'm going to have to see some examples of play. Like Gumshoe, it sounds like you're solving a problem that I and my group don't have. Unlike Gumshoe, you're solving it by adding a resource the Director has to track.<br /> <br /> Sardonyx doesn't have to be for me and mine, of course. I'll still pick up the Trinity book for background and convert it to Fate Core.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T08:37:36-07:00","id":545341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=544506#post544506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if that's true for all groups / GM's (which I don't agree with just from my own experience), I'm still not convinced that more dice / mechanics is the way to go for every time a dice roll doesn't come out in a character's favor - and I actively dislike when those mechanics require tracking one or more pools which can subsequently be spent on x, y or z options. Personal preference and all that. As a GM I prefer things like combat to be streamlined with little admin.<br /> <br /> As I've said, hopefully there's some way to make the concept of Momentum optional, or at the least a couple different (more streamlined) options for how the system handles fail-sideways / fail-forwards or whatever we're calling it if we have to have a system level process for it. Definitely something without pools to track and points to spend on effects. A simple bonus here or there, optionally, perhaps.<br /> <br /> I am really liking plenty of the other components of the system though such as how difficulty, target numbers and so on are handled. While only personally interested in the Aeon setting, I can see how tiered play will be a great way to handle scale in a setting like Aberrant - that'll be interesting to read more about. Hearing that Willpower has possibly been removed is very welcome news. There's a running joke with one group I've gamed with since the Vampire 1st came out that 'Willpower is just for looking at&quot;. So yeah, no loss there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in agreement with all this: tracking additional pools is a time-drain I don't want, optional systems are great for customization (although I suspect Momentum is going to be pretty baked into Sardonyx), and I'm liking almost all the other changes I'm seeing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T11:15:37-07:00","id":545556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=545337#post545337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess I'm going to have to see some examples of play. Like Gumshoe, it sounds like you're solving a problem that I and my group don't have. Unlike Gumshoe, you're solving it by adding a resource the Director has to track.<br /> <br /> Sardonyx doesn't have to be for me and mine, of course. I'll still pick up the Trinity book for background and convert it to Fate Core.</div> </div> </div> </div>So let me get this straight: your complaint about Sardonyx is that it requires you to track a resource (i.e., Momentum), and your solution is to switch to Fate Core, which is built around tracking a resource (i.e., Fate Points)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T12:17:11-07:00","id":545614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=545556#post545556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let me get this straight: your complaint about Sardonyx is that it requires you to track a resource (i.e., Momentum), and your solution is to switch to Fate Core, which is built around tracking a resource (i.e., Fate Points)?</div> </div> </div> </div>My complaint about Sardonyx is that Momentum is a resource that the Director must track in order to maximize the use of the NPCs -- I need to know how many are available in the pool, and how many my NPCs can use, and what strategies I need to do to get more in order to maintain the game's flow.<br /> <br /> In Fate Core, the fate points are in the players' hands. I don't have to track them, only use them as tool to push or pull the characters into interesting situations. I have an infinite supply for my NPCs if needed, so I don't need to worry about any of the resource management issues I would with Momentum.<br /> <br /> Make more sense?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T12:35:20-07:00","id":545645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=545556#post545556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let me get this straight: your complaint about Sardonyx is that it requires you to track a resource (i.e., Momentum), and your solution is to switch to Fate Core, which is built around tracking a resource (i.e., Fate Points)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not intending to answer for PaulChapman on this but I have some thoughts. Many things about those systems encourage fairly fast play so the impact of that pool is relatively minimal <i>in context</i>. Fate is a bit too abstract for me personally and I'll readily admit only having played it a couple of times, but I recognize how streamlined it is <i>overall</i>. I get a different vibe from the what we've seen of Sardonyx.<br /> <br /> It is interesting seeing the different views on all this (even if we fundamentally disagree on the value of some key points). It does remind me of the work that has to go into a new gaming system. Add dealing with clearly varying tastes of fans, its clear how much of a labor of love this must be for the writers / developers (thicks skins 'a must', etc). <br /> <br /> If my dislike of Momentum / Consolations comes over as harsh that's absolutely not the intent. As written, its just something that could be a dealbreaker for me if its not an optional mechanic - and I'll happily accept that's both my prerogative and also my 'problem'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> With that, I'll leave responding to any more points on Momentum until I've had a change to actually playtest it. <br /> <br /> Um, so....what about those target numbers, hey? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T12:37:58-07:00","id":545658,"title":"","content":"PaulChapman: Yes. Looks like your issue might be easily addressed by an optional rule to the effect of \u201cgive the Director an infinitely large red pool, and trust that he won't abuse it\u201d.<br /> <br /> Target numbers: was it this thread or the other one where I posted an excerpt from MCG? From a technical standpoint, I find that I like the lowering target number as a means of giving higher-tier characters more successes and a reduced chance of failure, rather than messing with the size of the pool. From an aesthetic standpoint, it still feels right; target number isn't a matter of difficulty; it's a matter of scale. <br /> <br /> And come to think of it, ISTR someone mentioning something about environmental factors playing into scale, with examples including things like a god of thunder effectively being in a higher tier in a thunderstorm or Batman's tier getting a boost when he's working with the Justice League. Let me hunt down a link, unless someone else beats me to it\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-08-2015, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T13:04:01-07:00","id":545694,"title":"","content":"That's Dave Brookshaw's quote (don't feel bad, Dataweaver, he said it while sitting right next to me). That refers to Myth Level, which is a <b>Scion</b> balancing mechanic, though I imagine it will be easy to rename and adopt for <b>Aberrant</b> (and potentially aberrants in <b>Aeon</b>, which happen to be written by some guy who's handsome).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T13:16:29-07:00","id":545709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=545658#post545658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PaulChapman: Yes. Looks like your issue might be easily addressed by an optional rule to the effect of \u201cgive the Director an infinitely large red pool, and trust that he won't abuse it\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps. I remain unconvinced that the overall mechanic of Momentum is needed. I don't recall a situation in my games where I would have been grateful for it's existence. Now, that could easily be a shortcoming of my own experience, but I'd much rather have mechanics that help spread the spotlight to the quiet players, or to help those who are reluctant to contribute story details.<br /> <br /> Again: my table may not necessarily be representative of a significant portion of the gaming tables in the marketplace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T16:09:03-07:00","id":545937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=545614#post545614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My complaint about Sardonyx is that Momentum is a resource that the Director must track in order to maximize the use of the NPCs</div> </div> </div> </div>I will state again that a resource indicated by a physical token, such as dice, is far easier to track than any of the other random things you are tracking, especially some of the things brought up as examples in this thread. (NPC ammo? Ain't nobody got time for that.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T17:52:12-07:00","id":546172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=545937#post545937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will state again that a resource indicated by a physical token, such as dice, is far easier to track than any of the other random things you are tracking, especially some of the things brought up as examples in this thread. (NPC ammo? Ain't nobody got time for that.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You got me: I rarely track ammo. But after running games for my group for 15 years, I have found some things interrupt my flow and some things don't. Trying to track fate points in Atomic Robo broke my flow (unlike Fate Core, GMs in AR have a fate point budget they must adhere to); tracking hit points, attack modifiers, damage, etc in D&amp;D5 doesn't.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T21:07:22-07:00","id":547963,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/codename-sardonyx-teaser-the-second/\" target=\"_blank\">Teaser the Second</a>: Attributes and Skills","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T22:18:18-07:00","id":547999,"title":"","content":"May I just say that I <i>vastly</i> prefer &quot;Grace&quot; to &quot;Manipulation&quot;? One of those words has a seriously negative charge for me, at least.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T22:53:36-07:00","id":548030,"title":"","content":"Yarp. I've had so much trouble breaking people of thinking manipulation as the &quot;evil&quot; stat... a hold over from cWoD I think, as new players (in my circles at least) have an easier time grasping that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T23:05:37-07:00","id":548039,"title":"","content":"Halfway through reading it\u2026 and I like it. A lot. Action/Adventure deals with the Physical Arena, where Might, Finesse, and Vitality dominate; Procedurals deal with the Mental Arena, where Reason, Cunning, and Discipline dominate; and Intrigue deals with the Social Arena, where Presence, Grace, and Poise dominate. The Power Function (Might, Reason, and Presence) is your ability to make things happen in that Arena; the Control Function (Finesse, Cunning, and Grace) is how aware you are and how well you adapt to changes in that Arena; and the Resistance Function (Vitality, Discipline, and Poise) is your ability to cope when things don't go your way in that Arena. <br /> <br /> Practical application: noticing things is <i>usually</i> in the Mental Arena, and thus based off of Cunning; but there are also cases of Physically noticing something (that is, your body, not your mind, does the noticing, allowing you to react without thinking), in which case you'd be using Finesse; and when you're dealing with Intrigue, you use your Grace to notice subtle emotional cues that tell you how the people around you are responding. <br /> <br /> EDIT: it seems to me that spotting trickery ought to be a matter of Cunning rather than Discipline. <br /> <br /> Also: <br /> \u2022 low Presence, low Grace: wallflower. <br /> \u2022 high Presence, low Grace: bull in a china shop \u2014 great at inspiring others, whether it be inspiring loyalty or fear; but <i>not</i> good at subtly. <br /> \u2022 low Presence, high Grace: effective at working behind the scenes; not so good when put in the spotlight. <br /> <br /> Now, on to Skills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-10-2015, 02:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T23:11:41-07:00","id":548042,"title":"","content":"My only &quot;What the...&quot; moment was that Tracking is Animal Ken instead of Survival. I don't see how being good with animals helps you track them <i>and people</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T23:26:25-07:00","id":548067,"title":"","content":"I'll be updating this post as I run across WTFs. <br /> <br /> Dodging: Vitality + Agility, not Finesse + Agility?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T23:31:06-07:00","id":548070,"title":"","content":"Remember: This is also open dev. While Neall may poke his head in here on occasion, if there's a specific issue you want to raise, the comments of the blog post may be a better place to bring it to his attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T23:36:07-07:00","id":548077,"title":"","content":"Ugh. I find the blog comments to be kludgey and irritating. But OK; if that's where you want your feedback, that's where I'll put it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T23:45:58-07:00","id":548089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=548067#post548067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be updating this post as I run across WTFs.<br /> <br /> Dodging: Vitality + Agility, not Finesse + Agility?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like that actually, You're vitality as survival instinct is a neat concept","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T00:14:20-07:00","id":548121,"title":"","content":"As an amateur game designer, I've been toying with a &quot;house system&quot; that's not unlike this one \u2014 the main difference being the die mechanic (our group prefers a fixed dice pool for all rolls, so we use a variant of 2d10 for everything). Another notion I've developed is splitting the Specialties into Fields and Feats (where Fields specify what you're dealing with and are almost always mandatory, with everyone getting one Field automatically; and Feats specify what sorts of things you do with the Skill and are almost always optional). I have a single \u201cFighting\u201d Skill that covers both Brawling and Weapons, the distinction being whether your initial Field is \u201cunarmed\u201d or a particular kind of weapon. Note that Feats such as Grappling <i>can</i> be done with weapons \u2014 if you have the right weapons (whips, chains, flails, police batons, etc.)<br /> <br /> One of the reasons I came up with the Fields concept is that it lets you create a concise skill list that's nonetheless easy to adapt to different settings: Feats tend to be fairly stable (and from a technical standpoint, one might say that Skills are defined primarily in terms of what their Feats are), but Fields are highly dependent on setting: the kinds of vehicles available in <b>Adventure!</b> are going to be very different from the kinds of vehicles available in <b>\u00c6on</b>. So you have one Pilot Skill, and the things you can do with it tend to be the same whether you live in the Roaring 20s or on 22nd-century Mars; but <i>what</i> you Pilot will change drastically between the two. Likewise, the Science Fields of the 22ns Century will be quite different from the Science Fields of the early 20th Century. Again, same skill; but very different feels based on what Fields are available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-10-2015, 06:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T06:43:05-07:00","id":548447,"title":"","content":"What's a Terat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T06:57:20-07:00","id":548458,"title":"","content":"My guess is that it's what the Terragen are seeking to become.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T06:59:15-07:00","id":548461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=548447#post548447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's a Terat?</div> </div> </div> </div>It comes from the Greek 'teras' - monster, prodigy. In 1e Aberrant, it was a term used for members of the Teragen. Neall posted over on the blog that he was using it here to refer to a nova at the very height of power and monstrosity, and was unaware it was already a setting term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T07:23:19-07:00","id":548524,"title":"","content":"No, I <i>vaguely </i>remembered. I just wanted to stress that I wasn't giving away some secret knowledge of Aberrant's setting, just setting a rough benchmark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T08:02:59-07:00","id":548559,"title":"","content":"Another thing that surprised me: Daredevils are a scion thing now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T08:28:08-07:00","id":548625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=548559#post548559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing that surprised me: Daredevils are a scion thing now?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, though that Tier roughly corresponds to pre-Visitation Scions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:07:02-07:00","id":548771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=548625#post548625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, though that Tier roughly corresponds to pre-Visitation Scions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiousity, is that the same level that sorcerers and the other non-Scion characters that are being introduced?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:10:15-07:00","id":548778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=548771#post548771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Out of curiousity, is that the same level that sorcerers and the other non-Scion characters that are being introduced?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, although sorcerers (in particular) and certain Legendary creatures have the option to scale up to Hero level or beyond in certain aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:57:11-07:00","id":549022,"title":"","content":"1) Pretty much love the system. Agree with Dataweaver that Vitality + Agility is an odd choice for Dodge, but that's easily house-ruled.<br /> <br /> 2) I can't help wondering what the &quot;creativity&quot; stat would be for, say, Performance (as opposed to doing well on the spot) -- IIRC, it used to be Wits, but I don't get that vibe from Cunning. &quot;Storytelling&quot; under Culture is Grace, but that's also live.<br /> <br /> 3) I know some folks will be less than happy at the broad applicability of Skills, but frankly I'm quite pleased. Being better in some areas than others seems to be governed largely by Attributes and Tricks; not sure how I feel about the semi-regular Attribute/Skill mixing (my players generally like to be able to look at one place to know what to roll), but it should be manageable.<br /> <br /> Also, I know this is another forum, but Scion + Mortal Sorcerers = YES. (I really wanted rules for them during my Scion game for cult leader types.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T14:31:17-07:00","id":549386,"title":"","content":"Vitality + Agility instead of Finesse does help remove the &quot;Dexterity = Godstat&quot; issue. Though we're going to have to see the combat system a bit to see how much sense it really makes.<br /> <br /> The preview makes sure there that Might is a valid offensive Attribute, and Vitality a valid defensive Attribute, meaning Finesse doesn't become the one you have to invest in if you want to be a combat heavy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T16:41:36-07:00","id":549510,"title":"","content":"It's interesting that the defenses of &quot;Dodge = Vitality + Agility&quot; all seem to be based on the notion that it provides a better balance of usefulness among the Attributes, rather than being based on the notion that using Vitality to Dodge <i>makes sense</i>, given the description of Vitality. Do the respective definitions of the Control and Resistance Functions need to be adjusted so that the latter includes an aptitude for reacting to danger?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T17:08:55-07:00","id":549524,"title":"","content":"Poise and Discipline will need further explaining as to why they are different. Pretty much expected that with the Power/Control/Resistance breakdown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T17:16:41-07:00","id":549528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=549510#post549510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's interesting that the defenses of &quot;Dodge = Vitality + Agility&quot; all seem to be based on the notion that it provides a better balance of usefulness among the Attributes, rather than being based on the notion that using Vitality to Dodge <i>makes sense</i>, given the description of Vitality.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know how the combat system works yet; and what it means to dodge in its context. So we can only look at things like the overall distribution of effects between Attributes and Skills.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T20:21:29-07:00","id":549636,"title":"","content":"Right; but my point is that the uses of the Attributes should flow naturally from their descriptions; if they don't, then either the usage should change or the descriptions should. Or a bit of both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T23:01:40-07:00","id":549801,"title":"","content":"Then shouldn't your question be, &quot;Why not Cunning + Agility?&quot;<br /> <br /> Cunning talks about reacting quickly, and responding to your environment. Finesse talks about how precise you are.<br /> <br /> Vitality does actually say that it involves being harder to harm. As well, dodging, which generally means much larger body movements than blocking/parrying an attack, is more draining; another thing Vitality is supposed to inform you about how well you deal with. A character that's throwing their body out of the way tries out and gets hit sooner if they have low stamina to keep it up.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, esp. given the nature of this document, we can easily read more or less into the text to say, &quot;This makes perfect sense,&quot; or &quot;This doesn't make sense.&quot; and there isn't a greater context to judge those readings by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T15:28:42-07:00","id":550816,"title":"","content":"And do we use Integrity, Larceny, or Persuasion to lie? So hard to say, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T18:03:12-07:00","id":550931,"title":"","content":"I've submitted a suggestion that \u201ctell a lie\u201d be replaced by something to the effect of \u201cconvey sincerity\u201d; that is remove the implicit assumption that you\u2019re using the skill to deceive. My reasoning is two-fold: <br /> <br /> First, Sardonyx is aiming for a more positive tone than the Storyteller/ing systems have; it's why you have Grace rather than Manipulation. &quot;Convincing someone that you're on the level&quot; is a more positive way of looking at things than \u201clying\u201d. And it's a better fit for Integrity. <br /> <br /> Second, it has a wider application. \u201cLying\u201d only comes into play when you're trying to deceive someone; \u201cconvey trustworthiness\u201d comes into play any time someone has reason to doubt you. That <i>includes</i> situations where you're trying to lie; but it also includes situations where someone else has besmirched your character (or circumstances have brought your honesty into question) and you're trying to defend your good name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T18:12:34-07:00","id":550935,"title":"","content":"BTW, I vastly prefer seeing Attributes grouped by Function rather than by Arena, at least in terms of how they're described; because where confusion between Attributes comes up, it's more likely to involve same Function, different Arenas (e.g., Cunning vs. Grace, or Discipline vs. Poise) than same Arena, different Functions. Putting the descriptions of the hard-to-distinguish ones side by side makes the necessary compare-and-contrast much more natural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T19:58:30-07:00","id":551017,"title":"","content":"Also, I have some issues with some of the Attribute naming choices. Cunning, in particular: it means &quot;the skill of achieving one's ends through deceit&quot;. <i>Not</i> what the Control Function in the Mental Arena is described as. Really, Wits is a near-perfect name for it; the only downside to Wits is that you appear to be making an effort to avoid reusing Attribute names that Storyteller/ing used. So if Wits is out, what about something like Intuitioin, Awareness, Insight, or Acumen? Again, Wits would be best; but any of these others would be better than Cunning, at least IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T04:38:13-07:00","id":551263,"title":"","content":"Cunning also means ingenuity, and doesn't necessarily mean deceitfulness exclusively. When we say someone is a man of great cunning, we mean someone who is clever, skillful, or resourceful; such a person is probably not above deception but we aren't flat calling them a liar. I might like to be called a cunning businesswoman but I don't think I'd like to be called a lying bitch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T11:28:10-07:00","id":551876,"title":"","content":"A wolf is a cunning predator, it is not a deceitful hunter","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T02:13:19-07:00","id":554063,"title":"","content":"Belatedly, i don't think i can add much to the discussion here, except to express my continued interest. There just wasn't enough for me to get the dice out and play-test, so i have to reserve judgement. But i'm terribly interested to see where you go with this framework.<br /> Perhaps i'll add more when i've read the replies in this thread thoroughly. But i'll just be picking at details if i do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T09:42:52-07:00","id":554452,"title":"","content":"I'm certainly very excited. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T16:42:59-07:00","id":557510,"title":"","content":"So far, I would say Reason and Cunning both pair well with every skill. Some are slightly more offbeat uses, but almost everything works with those two; Reason+Agility is a bit hard to justify but everything else seems to work, and Cunning pairs with everything.<br /> <br /> Might is one of the hardest to pair. Right now, I can see it working with Agility (Parkour), Aim (Hucking Stuff), Analyze (Breaking Stuff), Athletics (Lifting/Climbing/Swimming/Everything), Brawl (Hulk Smash), Performance (Flexing and various feats of strength), Persuasion (Intimidation), Pilot (certain muscle-powered vehicles, like bikes, might benefit from Might+Pilot), maybe Survival (Woodcutting? I'm not sure), maybe by a slim chance Technology (for very primitive tech, or or crafts that are strongly based on strength; blacksmithing might work), and Weaponry (Hulk Smash with indirect assistance from Chrysler Corporation). Finesse pairs better, although of course it's still a stretch for some things. The Resistance traits pair poorly across the board, but I kind of expected that.<br /> <br /> Vitality seems like it would be good for tasks that are physically exhausting, or where sleepiness or other such thing might come into play.<br /> Discipline seems like it would be good for tasks that are somewhat boring.<br /> Poise seems good for dealing with tasks that are frustrating or possibly frightening.<br /> <br /> Also, Performance is the little black dress of skills: it goes with everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","user":"Wolfgar","date":". 06-16-2015, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T16:55:06-07:00","id":557520,"title":"","content":"Wonder what's next. Edges? Perhaps some thoughts on combat.<br /> <br /> Right now I kind of favor the idea of having two offensive attributes, mainly Might and Finesse, and two defensive attributes, mainly Vitality and Cunning. Might gives you you strong attacks; Finesse gives you precision attacks. Cunning lets you dodge/block attacks, while Vitality would let you absorb/soak up attacks. Might is easy to dodge, but hard to soak. Finesse is easy to soak, but hard to dodge.<br /> <br /> It's mostly based on personal aesthetics over any sense of balance, and I should know better than to start developing any kind of expectation of how I would do it, but I'm fond of the idea for now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T18:35:57-07:00","id":557684,"title":"","content":"Might + Tech = Using a manual tool instead of a power tool? I've had to change a flat more than once, and loosening those lug nuts - especially if they were secured with an impact wrench without any care that you might have to get them loose without one - was a heck of a lot of brute force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T06:46:35-07:00","id":558186,"title":"","content":"True Story. I had to stand by and let my future wife loosen one once (she's 5 inches taller and had more leverage) cops came by and joined her in mocking me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T08:30:35-07:00","id":558293,"title":"","content":"Where's that 3rd teaser? He's a day late...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T10:12:45-07:00","id":558392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>karpomatic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=558293#post558293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's that 3rd teaser? He's a day late...</div> </div> </div> </div>He had trouble with allergies, so he delayed it a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T12:27:12-07:00","id":558538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>karpomatic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=558293#post558293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's that 3rd teaser? He's a day late...</div> </div> </div> </div>In my day, we took our teasers when we got 'em, and we were lucky to get a synopsis of the book we were gettin'. And we were <i>damn thankful </i>for it!<br /> <br /> No respect from today's gaming crowd, let me tells ya.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T12:37:43-07:00","id":558566,"title":"","content":"Not our fault you said &quot;Tuesday&quot; and &quot;lean and hungry&quot; #ThisIsOnYou","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T13:45:43-07:00","id":558657,"title":"","content":"Neall, im mailing you a costco sized variety bag of allergy meds, so this never happens again...tack it onto the eventual kickstarter...should I just mail it to OPP?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T13:47:01-07:00","id":558658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=558538#post558538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my day, we took our teasers when we got 'em, and we were lucky to get a synopsis of the book we were gettin'. And we were <i>damn thankful </i>for it!<br /> <br /> No respect from today's gaming crowd, let me tells ya.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Neall, stop telling us about how you walked in the snow uphill to school, both ways, tell those darn kids to get off your lawn, turn down that rock music and get a haircut, turn off your AOL and Compuserve, and get cracking on those spoilers!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T17:00:34-07:00","id":558865,"title":"","content":"And here I was just assuming it was an off week. I didn't see anything implicit saying we would get spoilers on Tuesday each week, every week for the foreseeable future...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T17:02:20-07:00","id":558866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=557684#post557684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might + Tech = Using a manual tool instead of a power tool? I've had to change a flat more than once, and loosening those lug nuts - especially if they were secured with an impact wrench without any care that you might have to get them loose without one - was a heck of a lot of brute force.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. Of course, some of it depends on how much your knowledge of machines and objects comes into it. Then again there is the need of drama - how often would it be dramatically interesting to roll to see if you can remove lugnuts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T17:50:11-07:00","id":558895,"title":"","content":"The principle is sound, though: any time nuts and bolts are cinched down too tightly (or you <i>want</i> them to be cinched down too tightly), Might + Tech would be a suitable choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T21:38:28-07:00","id":559044,"title":"","content":"It's also a scaling system. A mundane/daredevil might need to change a tire in a bind as a threat they could run into. &quot;The lugnuts are overtightened&quot; could easily be part of the problem.<br /> <br /> Sure it's not something I'd imagine higher tier PCs to worried about.... but I'm assuming they have stuff for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T21:51:58-07:00","id":559050,"title":"","content":"Teaser 3: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/codename-sardonyx-schemas-and-scales/\" target=\"_blank\">Schemas and Scales</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T23:26:39-07:00","id":559110,"title":"","content":"Commenting as I go\u2026<br /> <br /> Maybe, instead of \u201ccombat\u201d, it could be \u201caction sequence\u201d rules? \u201cCombat\u201d brings to mind an action sequence where violence plays a significant role; but chases, races, and defuse-the-bomb-before-it-goes-off all fit within the same structure of initiative, rounds, etc., without necessarily featuring violence per se. Heck, I could see using this for dynamic sports like basketball, soccer, and blitzball; and while hockey <i>can</i> get violent, that's generally something the referees discourage. <br /> <br /> \u201cCombat\u201d only covers a small slice of this; \u201caction sequence\u201d covers it all \u2014 and has something of a double meaning, being both a cinema term for scenes in an action/adventure show that feature action, and (taken a bit more literally) a sequence of actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T00:18:55-07:00","id":559125,"title":"","content":"Under &quot;Intrigue&quot;, I assume that &quot;Subtlety&quot; is a holdover from an earlier draft of the Attributes, and should now be Grace?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T00:29:12-07:00","id":559126,"title":"","content":"Okay. That is really really terrible scale. Either You failed naming again and this time extremely terribly-Titan is supposed to be high end god, or you do not get scale of these settings and we can call it a day. Defining ability of high end god in Scion is localized omnicide and being laws of physics for a limited time.Literal win buttons, that must be countered. You said several times, that you want to flatten the curve somewhat, so Psions do not look so laughable. Then you put Abberants over beings with this power level and not insignificantly so. How is this supposed to work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T01:02:40-07:00","id":559132,"title":"","content":"If Intensity is supposed to follow the Fibonacci Series, it should go 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, 21, 34, 55, and so on instead of 1, 2, 3, 5, 7, 12, 19, 31, 40, and so on. <br /> <br /> Also, how does Scale connect to Tier? Does each Tier define a maximum Scale that you can have? <br /> <br /> And my gut instinct is that I'd rather have Intensity and Magnitude baked directly into what your Effects give you instead of serving as a boost or multiplier to how many Effects you get: something more along the lines of &quot;a Scale 3 Might Effect lets you lift a Scale 3 object&quot;, as opposed to \u201cbecause your Might is Scale 3, multiply the number of Effects you generate by 5\u201d. The principles of MCG's scaling system are nice; but I was hoping that Sardonyx would show a bit more\u2026 finesse in deploying it. <br /> <br /> Finally, I'm not comfortable with saying that Trinity's Aberrants outclass Scion's Gods. The former are, after all, <i>gods</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T01:04:14-07:00","id":559133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559126#post559126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. That is really really terrible scale. Either You failed naming again and this time extremely terribly-Titan is supposed to be high end god, or you do not get scale of these settings and we can call it a day. Defining ability of high end god in Scion is localized omnicide and being laws of physics for a limited time.Literal win buttons, that must be countered. You said several times, that you want to flatten the curve somewhat, so Psions do not look so laughable. Then you put Abberants over beings with this power level and not insignificantly so. How is this supposed to work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Note the 'Intensity vs Magnitude' subsection: &quot;This system shoots realism out the window with a cannon, and for a good reason: encounters of differing scale need to be survivable, even if only by the slimmest margin'. Ain't no-one getting an automatic win button purely on Scale.<br /> <br /> Also note Neall's comment that this is their best guess at the uppermost powers of a Tier, and shouldn't be taken as indicative of their respective games.<br /> <br /> The example Aberrants Neall cites as making the gods feel limited are Divis Mal and the Colony. Given how long <i>those</i> guys have been around by the Aeon era, they should be god-like or beyond.<br /> <br /> And Titan <i>avatars</i> are high-end gods. The Titans themselves take on pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 06-18-2015, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T01:33:11-07:00","id":559146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559133#post559133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note the 'Intensity vs Magnitude' subsection: &quot;This system shoots realism out the window with a cannon, and for a good reason: encounters of differing scale need to be survivable, even if only by the slimmest margin'. Ain't no-one getting an automatic win button purely on Scale.<br /> <br /> Also note Neall's comment that this is their best guess at the uppermost powers of a Tier, and shouldn't be taken as indicative of their respective games.<br /> <br /> The example Aberrants Neall cites as making the gods feel limited are Divis Mal and the Colony. Given how long <i>those</i> guys have been around by the Aeon era, they should be god-like or beyond.<br /> <br /> And Titan <i>avatars</i> are high-end gods. The Titans themselves take on pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but Scale still should be contextually able to represent differing power levels and contextually Colony over beings, whose core and frankly defining ability is push button omnicide does not work, because there is not fight, even if we go and go with just cinematic representation. <br /> <br /> Colony shows, colony one shots Earth- heroes cinematicaly survive is not a good story. I know this is Trinity forum, but this does completely ignore high end gods. They are supposed to be Universe killers by mythology and story.<br /> <br /> Your point about differing Titan terms is the issue, Titan Avartars fight Pantheons Titans themselves are unfightable, because they are laws of physics 24 hours a day and they supersede Gods.<br /> <br /> Outside of this discussion Titan as the top tier is crappy name, because it does not define which titan and should be changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T04:00:42-07:00","id":559212,"title":"","content":"As we keep saying, the names for tiers (and some mechanics) are placeholders, ready to be naturalized into Trinity or Scion. Getting hung up on the name for the top scale when neither game will present the scale table like that isn't really useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T05:30:06-07:00","id":559271,"title":"","content":"I'm more hung up on how narrativist the system is, and how incoherent that makes the combat seem. You are the hero so you survive attacks that straight up kill dozens of other people per success? That doesn't make sense to me. You hit a guy with a heavy weapon and they are dead, not scraped around because they ate the designated badass normal.<br /> <br /> That would, actually, be fine for Adventure, but it's totally not for a postmodern supers game such as Aberrant. In Aberrant, Batman dies instantly when Thanosseid punches him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T05:51:00-07:00","id":559283,"title":"","content":"Double post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","user":"Solar","date":". 06-18-2015, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T06:38:49-07:00","id":559307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=558538#post558538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my day, we took our teasers when we got 'em, and we were lucky to get a synopsis of the book we were gettin'. And we were <i>damn thankful </i>for it!<br /> <br /> No respect from today's gaming crowd, let me tells ya.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hey, I'm damn thankful when the teasers get dropped. You've just got us chomping at the bit for more. I'm sure all also understand you are/were at the mercy of the Lord of Pollen. <br /> <br /> That being said, Does anyone else think how the initiative order is determined is funky?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T06:54:07-07:00","id":559321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559271#post559271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more hung up on how narrativist the system is . . .</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheTeaser</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This system shoots realism out the window with a cannon . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>That ship has sailed.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T09:30:45-07:00","id":559485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559271#post559271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would, actually, be fine for Adventure, but it's totally not for a postmodern supers game such as Aberrant. In Aberrant, Batman dies instantly when Thanosseid punches him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am relatively okay with that. I do prefer more cinematic take, unless it gets silly, sadly it often does, but the Adventure as the core inspiration to make this was here from the get go. One of the devs is on the record saying, that he disliked Abberant power levels and significantly preferred Adventure and if you read dev quotes, Imo it gets very clear, that Abberant is the setting led beyond the shed to make game line much more in line with Adventure more optimistic take. To me this was take on the Trinity Continuum from the get go and how much game loses by it is debatable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6491,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","user":"zorb42","date":". 06-18-2015, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T09:49:31-07:00","id":559495,"title":"","content":"This. I'm pretty sure that Aberrant 2e will be playing to a wider set of gameplay styles than 1e did, and that's fine by me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T10:21:14-07:00","id":559521,"title":"","content":"That's my gathering too. Aberrant was as I gather written with a very antagonistic vein towards the rest of the entire Continuum as an idea. This is not the case now; it's being written more as part of the whole. And part of that seems to be that there's a very narrow way to run Aberrant where it's pretty much the one-shotted and the not-one-shotted-as-quickly, and then there's soemthing that admits it's actually a game that's trying to emulate something and be something people play instead of as I gather worship of rocket tennis as if it is some post-modern statement I guess.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T10:25:55-07:00","id":559524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559271#post559271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more hung up on how narrativist the system is, and how incoherent that makes the combat seem. You are the hero so you survive attacks that straight up kill dozens of other people per success? That doesn't make sense to me. You hit a guy with a heavy weapon and they are dead, not scraped around because they ate the designated badass normal.<br /> <br /> That would, actually, be fine for Adventure, but it's totally not for a postmodern supers game such as Aberrant. In Aberrant, Batman dies instantly when Thanosseid punches him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman probably still dies--Scale provides *limited* charity for PCs. What Scale assumes is that PCs always get the lucky break that provides the possibility of survival and meaningful interaction. That means we assume &quot;Batman&quot; gets clipped, not hit full on. That means PCs drop under wreckage against an orbital laser. The laser still might kill them, but it isn't a totally foregone conclusion, which would be uninteresting.<br /> <br /> One relevant example is in Captain America: The Winter Soldier. That sub-treatment of the Marvel Cinematic Universe is fairly gritty, but Cap and Black Widow survive a cruise missile strike. They avoid being crushed by debris. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T10:31:37-07:00","id":559530,"title":"","content":"Aberrant 2e is whatever the authors want it to be.<br /> <br /> I'm sure they're aware that there are some 1e fans that will not be happy if 2e does not follow all of 1e's setting and style assumptions. But Aberrant 1e doesn't magically stop existing (and frankly it doesn't sound like the Sardonyx system is incapable of being dialed in to recapture whatever people want in to make it more 1e-like), and what really matters is Aberrant 2e being a really good game; not a game that clutches to every sacred cow of the last edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T10:38:57-07:00","id":559537,"title":"","content":"If the narrative protection / plot armor currently provided to PC's and other important characters is a problem in a particular setting, couldn't you simply apply the larger Magnitude multipliers against them, rather than only against minor characters and objects, to reflect greater &quot;realism&quot; in less cinematic circumstances?<br /> <br /> If you want Batman to become chunky salsa if hit by a god, the rules already seem to permit it. They system appears to just provide mechanics to allow, not mandate, more cinematic circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 06-18-2015, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T11:57:50-07:00","id":559630,"title":"","content":"OK.... I've skimmed through enough of this, but haven't read every word.<br /> <br /> I think I have a feel for where this is going, and some components of the other previews make a bit more sense tonally now. This isn't just giving <i>options</i> for cinematic play - cinematic play appears to be <i>the point</i>. Momentum / fail-sideways, players getting to choose who goes next in initiative, Focus, how scaling appears to work as just some examples - I can see what OPP is going for here the more I read.<br /> <br /> I keep thinking of the Avengers movies action sequences as I read through the various mechanics. And that's not a good thing.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, what Im seeing is too clunky for my tastes. There are some specifics I really welcome (target numbers is done well, as just one example), but Sardonyx is appealing to me less with each preview. For example, I would completely change how initiative works to ditch dice pools (more dice = slower combat), and I'm not interested in the players choosing which player goes after them - there are so many issues with that concept.<br /> <br /> Also, Marvel style action-hero tones are uninteresting to me and not remotely a good fit for how I interpret the Aeon setting, so lots of this doesn't do it for me at all (read: Momentum).<br /> <br /> Its a shame, I was hoping for something streamlined that allows each setting to emphasize their own unique tones. I'm not feeling that with the mechanics, and I suspect setting material (unless some core mechanics variants are provided) won't change this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T12:01:34-07:00","id":559636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559530#post559530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aberrant 2e is whatever the authors want it to be.<br /> <br /> I'm sure they're aware that there are some 1e fans that will not be happy if 2e does not follow all of 1e's setting and style assumptions. But Aberrant 1e doesn't magically stop existing (and frankly it doesn't sound like the Sardonyx system is incapable of being dialed in to recapture whatever people want in to make it more 1e-like), and what really matters is Aberrant 2e being a really good game; not a game that clutches to every sacred cow of the last edition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you.<br /> <br /> A lot of the objection in the vein of &quot;this isn't what Aberrant is about&quot; is based on individual interpretations of the original edition of Aberrant, which is not necessarily how we are interpreting the new edition of Aberrant. It seems to be fairly easy to tweak the rules how you like them in any case, but do not assume that because you played Aberrant 1e one way that TC:Aberrant necessarily must be designed the same way.<br /> <br /> Part of my mandate for the Continuum was to tweak all three lines to bring them into better harmony with each other, to create a true continuum. This is part of that. It's entirely possible that what we're doing may not be to everyone's tastes -- several people, like CHILL, have already said they don't want novas or Talents in their Aeon setting, and that's fine. Really! Once we release the games into the wild, everyone's free to splice it up however they like, and I'll be delighted to hear what people do with both setting and system when they're done. But we still have a specific direction we're going in to make the games we want to make. While I'm sure everyone would prefer that we're creating exactly the game they want, that's not possible, so we're creating the game <i>we</i> want, and hoping everyone else digs it (or at least finds enough to enjoy that they can ignore the bits they don't).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T13:01:25-07:00","id":559724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559485#post559485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am relatively okay with that. I do prefer more cinematic take, unless it gets silly, sadly it often does, but the Adventure as the core inspiration to make this was here from the get go. One of the devs is on the record saying, that he disliked Abberant power levels and significantly preferred Adventure and if you read dev quotes, Imo it gets very clear, that Abberant is the setting led beyond the shed to make game line much more in line with Adventure more optimistic take. To me this was take on the Trinity Continuum from the get go and how much game loses by it is debatable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only ever played Aberrant and despite it's flaws, what the devs dislike about it is what I like about it, in fact I think it's what makes it so good. Making it more like Adventure and such just seems to be a waste, and is what I was concerned about ever since they said they were going to bring the lines closer together.<br /> <br /> I guess I'll just step out if the Aberrant I loved is getting shelved, then. Not interested in playing another four colour derived modern comic system, to be honest. Those kinds of settings are a dime a dozen and a new system that does basically the same kind of supers as everyone else doesn't grab me at all.<br /> <br /> Very disappointed, to be honest. I was extremely excited for Aberrant 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","user":"Solar","date":". 06-18-2015, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T13:54:59-07:00","id":559764,"title":"","content":"So Chill and Solar, the purpose of us showing you these base rules sections now is to get useful feedback from our community before going down the road of making the system work in the first Trinity Continuum and Scion books. Seems like right now, you're extrapolating all the way to the finished books of the line you personally love and deciding they'll be bad for you, based on rules that are being fine tuned right now and which we haven't even worked up for your particular game yet. Am I misreading that? I'm just saying, maybe hang on a bit until we start previewing the actual games that you're interested in. <br /> <br /> Obviously, you're gonna do what you have to do, and I respect your right to decide, but that just makes sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T14:09:23-07:00","id":559795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I have a feel for where this is going, and some components of the other previews make a bit more sense tonally now. This isn't just giving <i>options</i> for cinematic play - cinematic play appears to be <i>the point</i>. Momentum / fail-sideways, players getting to choose who goes next in initiative, Focus, how scaling appears to work as just some examples - I can see what OPP is going for here the more I read.<br /> <br /> I keep thinking of the Avengers movies action sequences as I read through the various mechanics. And that's not a good thing.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, what Im seeing is too clunky for my tastes. There are some specifics I really welcome (target numbers is done well, as just one example), but Sardonyx is appealing to me less with each preview. For example, I would completely change how initiative works to ditch dice pools (more dice = slower combat), and I'm not interested in the players choosing which player goes after them - there are so many issues with that concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, Aeon has always had a Mass Effect vibe, partly because I played the first Mass Effect at the same time I read the original Aeon books bought in a collection of RPG.net.<br /> <br /> So...yeah, I wanted Aeon to feel a lot like Mass Effects 1 and 2. I'm confused as to what you think of are flaws in the initiative concept, but very well and good - to me, Aeon's always been a game of slick cinematics and MIDI-style music.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T14:19:09-07:00","id":559803,"title":"","content":"I do think there's room for a &quot;grim and gritty&quot;/deconstructionist dial for those who prefer Watchmen-esque <b>Aberrant</b> (and, if it's built into the core rules, it would also permit a variation of <b>\u00c6on</b> that feels more like <b>Aliens</b>, or a version of <b>Adventure!</b> that's more Noir than Pulp). But I'm personally fine with that being an option rather than the default, at least as far as how the core rules are written. If such an option is included in the core, then when they get around to writing <b>Aberrant</b> it would be reasonable to argue that <i>that one supplement</i> should default to deconstructionist rather than cinematic. But in the meantime, we've got <b>\u00c6on</b>, <b>Adventure!</b>, the modern-day Talents setting, and <b>Scion</b> that all tend to favor a more cinematic approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T14:30:07-07:00","id":559807,"title":"","content":"Okay, What are the opinions on focus? I do not want to sound as a big party pooper, but I do feel, that it is taking Cinematic concept slightly too literally. Camera is on you, therefore you will be better for this scene does not really appeal to me and it goes heavily against concept of simplicity. It is additional layer of bookkeeping. It is basically lot of tidly and rather specific bonuses, and it does not feel really rewarding. it is feels kinda empty overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T14:41:14-07:00","id":559811,"title":"","content":"Aeon was a pretty dark setting in and of itself. It was more in relief because your good guys were generally good guys, but it was still full of backstabbing, secrets, betrayals, and dystopias, and while I would say the tone of Aeon the organization changed with Aberrant, the tone of Aeon the game didn't. Not really. Assuming everything will be like Adventure is a bit premature.<br /> <br /> Also, holy quantum blue balls of Divis Mal this is a lot of material to chew through in one sitting. I'm gonna need some time to parse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T14:52:52-07:00","id":559815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559530#post559530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aberrant 2e is whatever the authors want it to be.<br /> <br /> I'm sure they're aware that there are some 1e fans that will not be happy if 2e does not follow all of 1e's setting and style assumptions. But Aberrant 1e doesn't magically stop existing (and frankly it doesn't sound like the Sardonyx system is incapable of being dialed in to recapture whatever people want in to make it more 1e-like), and what really matters is Aberrant 2e being a really good game; not a game that clutches to every sacred cow of the last edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>The counter is, of course it doesn't make sense to remake a property just to alienate fans of that property. Deciding to make remake Vampire the Masquerade to be about talking stuff toys that go on magical adventures in the realm of make-believe would probably be pointlessly antagonizing, even if it would be a cool game. That said, I'm sure the developers and writers are aware of this, and hopefully no one is stuck with the project who just, y'know, <i>hated</i> Aberrant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T14:54:09-07:00","id":559818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559524#post559524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Batman probably still dies--Scale provides *limited* charity for PCs. What Scale assumes is that PCs always get the lucky break that provides the possibility of survival and meaningful interaction. That means we assume &quot;Batman&quot; gets clipped, not hit full on. That means PCs drop under wreckage against an orbital laser. The laser still might kill them, but it isn't a totally foregone conclusion, which would be uninteresting.<br /> <br /> One relevant example is in Captain America: The Winter Soldier. That sub-treatment of the Marvel Cinematic Universe is fairly gritty, but Cap and Black Widow survive a cruise missile strike. They avoid being crushed by debris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, most settings seem to have this, in some form or fashion, even if it's only &quot;the hero is significantly fucked up rather than killed&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:11:18-07:00","id":559834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559815#post559815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The counter is, of course it doesn't make sense to remake a property just to alienate fans of that property. Deciding to make remake Vampire the Masquerade to be about talking stuff toys that go on magical adventures in the realm of make-believe would probably be pointlessly antagonizing, even if it would be a cool game. That said, I'm sure the developers and writers are aware of this, and hopefully no one is stuck with the project who just, y'know, <i>hated</i> Aberrant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a fan of Aberrant and had its bona fides in mind while working on this. But here's the thing: Aberrant often didn't do what its fiction said it did. So the situation you'd often get is yeah, sometimes Novas would paste each other, but sometimes the dice would be pretty underwhelming. Scaling is calibrated to that there's still fidelity to that fiction *and* there's a range of playable results. Testing the numbers and using plug-ins designed for specific games will refine things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":164,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","user":"Malcolm","date":". 06-18-2015, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:17:00-07:00","id":559843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559815#post559815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The counter is, of course it doesn't make sense to remake a property just to alienate fans of that property.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, but that doesn't really apply.<br /> <br /> Aberrant 2e isn't going to be a wildly different premise. But if you say, look at the difference between Forsaken 1e, and Forsaken 2e, people might not like the choices, but Forsaken 2e is still at its heart a Forsaken game. Even if it made massive changes in both system and tone from Forsaken 1e.<br /> <br /> Which is what we are most likely looking at in comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:23:53-07:00","id":559848,"title":"","content":"Okay, thoughts on this teaser, having reread this so I'm going off of more than my sleep addled thoughts from right before bed.<br /> <br /> I don't like the Initiative system. Now, there's obviously intended to be powers and what not that affect it, but going off the base system from the teaser the only thing that matters is who wins. After that, it doesn't matter who came in second or third or whatever. After the winner goes, then they hand it off to the Director(or vice versa), then they pick who goes next, etc. How well or how poorly you rolled doesn't really seem to have any effect if you're not the one who won.<br /> <br /> Focus......I just don't like Focus. Not my cup of tea.<br /> <br /> Then we've got Scale. I get what is intended with this and I appreciate that you're coming out and saying outright that it isn't supposed to be realistic, in so far as such a term applies when quantum powered super heroes and mystical deities are involved. I also understand and appreciate the stated reasoning, that encounters must be survivable instead of &quot;Your characters run into the wrong Giant and get stomped flat. GG&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, I dislike the sort of divide proposed, where a monster doesn't hit as hard when fighting a PC or when an attack that could slag a tank hits the Mystery Machine and it's still in one piece. Now, if there were in universe mitigating factors, like say, you're the child of a death god and are leveraging the power of your blood to sap a monster's vitality or the Mystery Machine is equipped with a forcefield, I'm fine with it.<br /> <br /> I just dislike it when the mitigating factor is &quot;Because you're a PC.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Last note, uh,...the math for the Scale Table seems to be off. It says to add the previous two Factors together to get the Intensity for the next level. Scale 5 for Proxies is +5 and the previous levels were +3 and +2. Scale 6 for Demigods should be 8(5+3), but it's listed as +7, which affects all of the numbers from that point on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:43:19-07:00","id":559869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559764#post559764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Chill and Solar, the purpose of us showing you these base rules sections now is to get useful feedback from our community before going down the road of making the system work in the first Trinity Continuum and Scion books. Seems like right now, you're extrapolating all the way to the finished books of the line you personally love and deciding they'll be bad for you, based on rules that are being fine tuned right now and which we haven't even worked up for your particular game yet. Am I misreading that? I'm just saying, maybe hang on a bit until we start previewing the actual games that you're interested in. Obviously, you're gonna do what you have to do, and I respect your right to decide, but that just makes sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey Rich, thanks for replying.<br /> <br /> I can't speak for Solar but no, that's not what I'm doing - yes you are misreading that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> I know my tastes well enough and have been gaming long enough to know what won't do it for me.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure i've stated several times that as far as I can see from what we've had made available to us to date, there's a handful of items that don't do it for me at a systems mechanics level and one of them is deal-breaker for me (as written). I have no idea how much, if any, of what's been released in the teasers will make it into each game. However, I know for certain that (again based on what I've seen so far) there are some mechanics that are a turn off for me, the major one being the entire momentum and momentum pools concept which does appear baked in fairly heavily. <br /> <br /> I did state in an earlier post somewhere that I would love to see an option for avoiding this concept entirely, which you may have missed. I'm not suggesting I wouldn't play Aeon because of the rules items I'm not liking - I'm saying I wouldn't play <i><b>any</b></i> games system with those items left intact.<br /> <br /> If they change to be more streamlined, and/or if they become optional and if I can easily write-out the minor items that don't do it for me (initiative, which I'll get to in a moment) then great. I can work around. If not, no problem I can use another system or use 1st ed, etc <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:59:32-07:00","id":559924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559764#post559764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Chill and Solar, the purpose of us showing you these base rules sections now is to get useful feedback from our community before going down the road of making the system work in the first Trinity Continuum and Scion books. Seems like right now, you're extrapolating all the way to the finished books of the line you personally love and deciding they'll be bad for you, based on rules that are being fine tuned right now and which we haven't even worked up for your particular game yet. Am I misreading that? I'm just saying, maybe hang on a bit until we start previewing the actual games that you're interested in.<br /> <br /> Obviously, you're gonna do what you have to do, and I respect your right to decide, but that just makes sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>All I can do is really comment on what is put in front of me at any given time.<br /> <br /> The thing is, what I am being told about what the devs aim to do and what the mandate is for the overall system just doesn't sound like it wants me to run and play games in my preferred style, in fact it seems that it is actively <i>against</i> that style. What I am saying in terms of the scale not feeling right for Aberrant, and not feeling like the narrativist ideals of the system are suitable for the setting, that's not stuff that seems to be part of the optional elements of the system. It's baked in as an ideal from day one. I raised this issue, and was told to wait for the scaling rules to come out, as those rules would alleviate my concerns. They have not alleviated my concerns.<br /> <br /> Sardonyx, no matter what it is intended for now, is intended for Aberrant at some point. I don't care about Adventure, and I'm not really bothered about Aeon, but I do care about Aberrant. So if you put it in front of me, with that in mind, I'm going assess it in terms of what I actually want it to do. After all, Aberrant is one of my favourite WW games ever.<br /> <br /> Which was, in fact, mostly due to that Aberrant was, in a good and proper sense of the word, <i>edgy.</i> It said &quot;you know what, super strength guy? If you punch this baseline, no matter who they are, <i>you will kill them</i>&quot; That was... hugely important to everything Aberrant said about what it meant to be a Nova. You had the powers of a God. You could change the world. But the world is a fragile and delicate thing, made of people who tore like paper when you unleashed your power within their vicinity, never mind <i>at</i> them. If you were in any way a moral person, you had to be incredibly disciplined in what you did and how you did it..<br /> <br /> A baseline, no matter how heroic, could never hope to a fight a Nova whose powers were related to combat, no matter how villainous. And that was kind of the key, in the sense that the world of Aberrant was not one where heroes won because they were heroes. Being a hero means nothing when you get splattered by a few hundred tons of force behind a fist that goes through your skull a a few hundred miles an hour. It didn't matter that things like that were unfair, or harsh, because like in the real world, power can be unfair and it can be harsh and it can destroy people, good people, if not used responsibly and ethically. And that was why Aberrant was cool, and different, because it actually took a look a superpowers that made them seem <i>powerful</i>, terrifyingly so.<br /> <br /> The system we have here says that if a plot designated hero has the camera on them then they get all these narrative bonuses that let them ignore those harsh realities, with incoherencies where a Nova can annihilate a fleet of armoured cars when they are crewed by randoms but struggle to trash one just because it contains a designated plot relevant individual. And that's great! For Adventure and Aeon and stuff, that works fine. <i>But not for Aberrant.</i> And I ask, if you're not going to do Aberrant with those harsh realities, <i>what the hell is the point of even calling it Aberrant?</i> Why even bother using the name and the setting, if you're going to just make it like every other modern superhero comic based setting that originated from four colour silver and golden age comics (which I love, I own over three hundred modern Marvel graphic novels, I just think that Aberrant doesn't and shouldn't try to be those things).<br /> <br /> I dunno. I love Aberrant. I never thought like I ran or played it in any kind of unusual or fringe way, I always thought that this was the true, genuine core of the game, the ethics of being a superhuman in a world which takes a more realistic assessment of how your powers would affect it. If you add narrativist protection for a heroic SWAT team guy who goes in to take down a Terat bad guy, then you're taking away from the core themes of the game, because really that guy should be SWAT-ted (couldn't resist) regardless of how brave or whatever he is. And as a Nova, you then have to shoulder the responsibility of being the guy who actually has to take action here or watch that SWAT team die. That happened, in a game I played, and it was really cool and really integral to how I see the setting. But what the scene (the death of a brave and heroic individual to a piece of shit asshole with some superpowers because life is not fair) showcases is what the system seems to be actively trying to work against, here.<br /> <br /> But from what I can tell, none of the developers want that. Which confuses and disappoints me. Because I really like that game, and I feel like I'm being alienated in favour of a new way of doing things just to make it fit with other games that I neither care about or play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T16:04:28-07:00","id":559936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559795#post559795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> To me, Aeon has always had a Mass Effect vibe, partly because I played the first Mass Effect at the same time I read the original Aeon books bought in a collection of RPG.net. So...yeah, I wanted Aeon to feel a lot like Mass Effects 1 and 2. I'm confused as to what you think of are flaws in the initiative concept, but very well and good - to me, Aeon's always been a game of slick cinematics and MIDI-style music.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see the Mass Effect vibe to some degree, sure. Aeon was always fairly dark in my interpretations though, and while details may change generally that's what drew me to the setting concept in the first place. I never read felt that Aeon was a game of slick cinematics (in terms of game-play) - we take completely different things away from Aeon, clearly. <br /> <br /> On initiative, I will never run with the idea of a player picking which player goes after them. There are two reasons. First, it doesn't really reflect on the capabilities of each individual character and feels somewhat arbitrary. Second, I know players who are always a lot quieter or less experienced who are going to end up being the last one picked. Sure, there's a mechanism in there to compensate for but I'd prefer not to have that problem in the first place to need compensation (hence the clunky comment earlier). That is easy to fix though, I'll just throw it out and go with something that doesn't require players to decide when other players act. There's a handful of items that I can easily change, initiative is one of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:12:38-07:00","id":559988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559834#post559834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a fan of Aberrant and had its bona fides in mind while working on this. But here's the thing: Aberrant often didn't do what its fiction said it did. So the situation you'd often get is yeah, sometimes Novas would paste each other, but sometimes the dice would be pretty underwhelming. Scaling is calibrated to that there's still fidelity to that fiction *and* there's a range of playable results. Testing the numbers and using plug-ins designed for specific games will refine things.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who has issues with some of WW/OPP's other properties, I know how frustrating it is to say &quot;this isn't the game I wanted&quot; while other folks are going &quot;but this is awesome!&quot;, so I sympathize. That said...THIS. Lots of powers were not calibrated to each other, especially combat powers (though social powers could be pretty weird too). I can't wait to see what TC: Aberrant looks like. (It might not even be called Aberrant! It's like calling an X-Men game &quot;Muties.&quot; That has power, but it's also weirdly off-putting to me as someone who's <i>also</i> a fan of Trinity.)<br /> <br /> On a more general note, it's clear that Continuum's going to be calibrated to the existence of all three major splats from the get-go, which was a huge problem for the old setting from day one. The Aeon Society photo in Trinity clearly demonstrated the setting's pulp roots, and we got teased Novas and Daredevils from the beginning. Problem was, none of the eras gelled with each other, and they were obviously intended to at the beginning. I love all three games, but outside of Adventure! (where Stalwarts and Mesmerists were, necessarily, flickering shadows of their descendents' might), each was -- and <i>had to be </i>-- its own thing. That was a problem, and right now, Sardonyx looks like the solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T19:12:59-07:00","id":560201,"title":"","content":"The thing is, the &quot;solution&quot; that was concocted for why Aberrant was so out of step with Adventure and Trinity (the whole business about separate timelines, one with a heroic quality and the other without) looks to still be a valid possibility in the Trinity Continuum. I really do hope that some effort is made toward arranging for the Sardonyx system to be able to survive having some of its narrativist tendencies removed by those who don't like them. Focus, for instance, feels clunky to me; and just for the sake of being able to streamline the gameplay, I'm hoping that it doesn't become so rooted in the core of the game that removing it leaves gaping holes in other crucial rules. <br /> <br /> For instance, it currently appears like Focus is closely tied to expending Momentum, if I'm reading things right; that is, the premise appears to be that you bide your time, building up a Black Pool, until someone hands you the Focus, at which point you burn through it to get the payoff for your patience. Taking Focus out of the picture removes the &quot;payoff&quot; from the picture. Or am I misreading something here?<br /> <br /> I wonder if \u201cthe deconstructionist side of the Continuum\u201d will end up being my first system hack\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-18-2015, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:01:03-07:00","id":560259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559843#post559843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, but that doesn't really apply.<br /> <br /> Aberrant 2e isn't going to be a wildly different premise. But if you say, look at the difference between Forsaken 1e, and Forsaken 2e, people might not like the choices, but Forsaken 2e is still at its heart a Forsaken game. Even if it made massive changes in both system and tone from Forsaken 1e.<br /> <br /> Which is what we are most likely looking at in comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say Forsaken 2nd isn't all that much a shift in tone so much as the system shifted more to what the tone was trying to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:17:04-07:00","id":560271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=560201#post560201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, the &quot;solution&quot; that was concocted for why Aberrant was so out of step with Adventure and Trinity (the whole business about separate timelines, one with a heroic quality and the other without) looks to still be a valid possibility in the Trinity Continuum. I really do hope that some effort is made toward arranging for the Sardonyx system to be able to survive having some of its narrativist tendencies removed by those who don't like them.</div> </div> </div> </div>All three games have very different feels to me. Trinity is a dark, post-apocalyptic place -- too dark for me at times, and a world where &quot;kill the muties&quot; is not only acceptable, but a <i>core setting assumption</i> that some hardcore Trinity fans complain about the dilution of -- but with pieces of hope scattered among the ruins. Aberrant is wry superhero satire where the Justice League has been infiltrated by the Technocracy, the Mutant Brotherhood is evolving beyond a frustrated Magneto, and most other Novas work for the highest bidder -- and again, hope is a wounded survivor. Adventure! is a gonzo pulp universe set in a 20s that never was, but should have been (most pulp comes from the 30s, but this way we avoid Depression depression) with crazy-awesome weird science and a League of Extraordinary Gentlement led by Doc Eon, where hope is very much alive (yet overshadowed by dark futures yet to be). Really, <i>none</i> of them fit each other -- which actually makes sense when you look at RL history, but if you want consistent mechanics things have to change. I freely admit a bias towards the Adventure!/&quot;World of Brightness&quot; concept they're going for, but when you have characters like Max Mercer and Danger Ace/Jake Danger surviving from game to game, it helps to have a way to get all the systems to play nice without slaughtering entire character concepts. (I don't count Michael/Primoris/Mal because his transformation is so fundamental to the jump from Adventure! to Aberrant.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=560201#post560201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Focus, for instance, feels clunky to me; and just for the sake of being able to streamline the gameplay, I'm hoping that it doesn't become so rooted in the core of the game that removing it leaves gaping holes in other crucial rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this one I'll grant you. I'm a big fan of Momentum and Scale variation (personally, I think the bonuses for main characters are <i>too</i> large at the upper end, having watched my Scion game collapse under the weight of Epic Attributes until I house-ruled them), but Focus could get clunky if poorly applied. We'll see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":2434,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","user":"Captain Aeon","date":"for clarity 06-18-2015, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:19:48-07:00","id":560272,"title":"","content":"Okay, before I dig into any really criticisms, I have to say I enjoy the Information Gathering system presented. I think it's robust without being too complex, and offers fairly solid advice. It seems to work for good utility. I don't think much needs to change about it in the final form.<br /> <br /> Secondly there is this: <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, social actions as a form of \u201ccombat,\u201d is not the core element of the system, but only one category. You don\u2019t overpower someone to make friends with them or fall in love. That\u2019s why social systems include cooperative and collective action. Systems should avoid modeling all social interactions as combat or imposing power over another. The manipulation system (see \u201cManipulation\u201d) covers that aspect of social play, but does not define it. </div> </div> </div><i>Thank you.</i> It's really refreshing to see someone both trying to make an in-depth social system without feeling the need to make it a 1-1 analog to the combat system, which almost never works in my opinion.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:59:13-07:00","id":560309,"title":"","content":"Initiative order is going to produce some weird results. It's also a little difficult to parse. Basically, tick order really doesn't matter for PCs, except to see if they beat any NPCs. After that, it doesn't matter. Tick order only matter for Director characters. Given the way the system functions, I wouldn't call them &quot;ticks&quot;. Ticks seem to imply a counting down and are more associated with some of the older Exalted systems. Here I might call it &quot;Priority&quot; of something instead.<br /> <br /> We will have some weird situations, like if we have a really slow. powerful NPC opponent - a glacier as they are sometimes called - they will always get to go before the rest of the party. They may not get to go before one guy...but everyone else is just out of luck, even if they are normally a lot faster. We also have situations where PCs aren't handing off to people who should be faster until later, which may seem weird. Then again, it may not be so bad with the base system, plus we still have kewl powerz to expect.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure what <b>Fields</b> bring to the table, or what exactly they are meant to do for the game. Right now, they look like a mostly unneeded complication, but I will accept some explanation from the crew on it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:01:06-07:00","id":560310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559630#post559630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would completely change how initiative works to ditch dice pools (more dice = slower combat), and I'm not interested in the players choosing which player goes after them - there are so many issues with that concept..</div> </div> </div> </div>From the look of things, I think you only ever really roll once. That shouldn't really slow things down appreciably.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:01:28-07:00","id":560311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Aeon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=560271#post560271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All three games have very different feels to me. Trinity is a dark, post-apocalyptic place -- too dark for me at times, and a world where &quot;kill the muties&quot; is not only acceptable, but a <i>core setting assumption</i> that some hardcore Trinity fans complain about the dilution of -- but with pieces of hope scattered among the ruins. Aberrant is wry superhero satire where the Justice League has been infiltrated by the Technocracy, the Mutant Brotherhood is evolving beyond a frustrated Magneto, and most other Novas work for the highest bidder -- and again, hope is a wounded survivor. Adventure! is a gonzo pulp universe set in a 20s that never was, but should have been (most pulp comes from the 30s, but this way we avoid Depression depression) with crazy-awesome weird science and a League of Extraordinary Gentlement led by Doc Eon, where hope is very much alive (yet overshadowed by dark futures yet to be). Really, <i>none</i> of them fit each other -- which actually makes sense when you look at RL history, but if you want consistent mechanics things have to change. I freely admit a bias towards the Adventure!/&quot;World of Brightness&quot; concept they're going for, but when you have characters like Max Mercer and Danger Ace/Jake Danger surviving from game to game, it helps to have a way to get all the systems to play nice without slaughtering entire character concepts. (I don't count Michael/Primoris/Mal because his transformation is so fundamental to the jump from Adventure! to Aberrant.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, don't get me wrong; a major element of the original trilogy was how Hope was featured across all three gamelines. I prefer to play the \u201cWorld of Hope\u201d side of the Continuum, and will not <i>personally</i> be offended if Aberrant and/or \u00c6on get a \u201cbecause heroism&quot; makeover. But my point is that it <i>is</i> a Continuum, and there ought to be room for the &quot;what would <i>really</i> happen if X?&quot; side of things that CHILL and Solar have been advocating. If that means that Aberrant, \u00c6on, and Adventure! all have their own feels, so be it (so long as a more cinematic playstyle can also be supported); if it means that all TC eras put cinematic reality at the heart of all eras, with deconstructionist options allowing you to tweak them for a harder setting if you prefer, that's also fine by me. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Aeon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=560271#post560271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, this one I'll grant you. I'm a big fan of Momentum and Scale variation (personally, I think the bonuses for main characters are <i>too</i> large at the upper end, having watched my Scion game collapse under the weight of Epic Attributes until I house-ruled them), but Focus could get clunky if poorly applied. We'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; I've mentioned elsewhere that I'm leery about the difference in Intensity for two adjacent levels of Scale ever exceeding 3; and a cap of 2 per level seems reasonable to me. Enhancements are a big deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:15:04-07:00","id":560345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=560311#post560311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah; I've mentioned elsewhere that I'm leery about the difference in Intensity for two adjacent levels of Scale ever exceeding 3; and a cap of 2 per level seems reasonable to me. Enhancements are a big deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same. It's really those big jumps that caused Epic Attributes to go so terribly wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T23:59:34-07:00","id":560496,"title":"","content":"Ticks if I remember right might be manipulated more with powers, but as is it is weird you don't really use the result much after the first roll. I would think that there'd be soem other way to do it or at least if it is so unimportant numerically to use something more like WoD Revised and Exalted 1e did where you just roll a d10 and add that to a base Initiative.<br /> <br /> The movement pool is weird to me since I don't know why it it has to be x2 after the pool. IN part since I'm not sure the order of operations ((Agiltiy + Athletics) x 2 or Agility + (Athletics x2)) and why the doubling of successes for Speed. Or what the fuck ou do wiht a Difficulty 0 roll normally unless there's environmental stuff after that I guess. I might just have missed something on that.<br /> <br /> Finally I kind of agree the scaling for Intensity is a tad worrisome at the higher levels. With Attributes and Skills being capped at poos of 12, unless there's a lot ot help in make-up for the success disparity like very low TNs, a difference of 12 successes (assuming the chart isn't fixed) between 9 and 8 is a tad ludicrous, since unless you have very low TNs at that tier, you're in effect getting flat out as many successes as their pool maxes out to on vaverage. This only exapserates just one Scale less than that.<br /> <br /> If that's the goal, it does it, but I do kind of wonder if the want to use the Fibonacci sequence is the best way to go save for a very limitted range that seems to break in half once you hit about 8+ for actual gamability. <br /> <br /> Which note is actually my main thing on the system and worries on being all post-modern and such. I am curious how wounds are handled, as that might impact things as well. As long as it's not like Exalted 2e rocket tag or nWoD's mugging simulator I'm sure things will end up well in trying to replicate what the games are trying to be in a fight at least and there seems to be enough emphasis on non-combat to make the success scale seem pretty great to me for those things.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T00:56:32-07:00","id":560514,"title":"","content":"You have to have at least 1 more success than the difficulty to pass the action. A difficulty 0 action means you need to have at least 1 success to make it (aka it's the easiest roll possible).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T05:56:42-07:00","id":560704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559936#post559936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see the Mass Effect vibe to some degree, sure. Aeon was always fairly dark in my interpretations though, and while details may change generally that's what drew me to the setting concept in the first place. I never read felt that Aeon was a game of slick cinematics (in terms of game-play) - we take completely different things away from Aeon, clearly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weird. I never saw Aeon as dark, or at least any darker than the real world. My games always had plenty of shiny space cities and high tech solutions, maybe to differentiate it from the Shadowrun games we played, which were filled with constant betrayals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559936#post559936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On initiative, I will never run with the idea of a player picking which player goes after them. There are two reasons. First, it doesn't really reflect on the capabilities of each individual character and feels somewhat arbitrary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having used a similar system in a Fate campaign or two, I agree that this form of initiative is divorced from the abilities of the characters. However, it does allow the players significantly more control over the pace of the conflict, so it doesn't feel arbitrary. In practice, you're passing the spotlight to the next logical player and setting up combos to take down the bad guys.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559936#post559936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, I know players who are always a lot quieter or less experienced who are going to end up being the last one picked. Sure, there's a mechanism in there to compensate for but I'd prefer not to have that problem in the first place to need compensation (hence the clunky comment earlier). That is easy to fix though, I'll just throw it out and go with something that doesn't require players to decide when other players act. There's a handful of items that I can easily change, initiative is one of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In the campaigns in which I've used / experienced the &quot;players choose who goes next&quot; initiative, we have a quiet player, a casual player, and a player who often forgets which floor the party is on. These players were not the last picked, because the more active/aggressive players were the ones doing the picking, and they'd chose the character that made the most sense to go next. If the coolest thing to happen right now would be for the brick to throw a barrel to distract the goon squad, setting up the others in the party to pick them off with blasters, then you hand the initiative to the brick, regardless of the activity level of the player.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T06:26:17-07:00","id":560726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=560496#post560496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ticks if I remember right might be manipulated more with powers, but as is it is weird you don't really use the result much after the first roll. I would think that there'd be soem other way to do it or at least if it is so unimportant numerically to use something more like WoD Revised and Exalted 1e did where you just roll a d10 and add that to a base Initiative.<br /> <br /> The movement pool is weird to me since I don't know why it it has to be x2 after the pool. IN part since I'm not sure the order of operations ((Agiltiy + Athletics) x 2 or Agility + (Athletics x2)) and why the doubling of successes for Speed. Or what the fuck ou do wiht a Difficulty 0 roll normally unless there's environmental stuff after that I guess. I might just have missed something on that.<br /> <br /> Finally I kind of agree the scaling for Intensity is a tad worrisome at the higher levels. With Attributes and Skills being capped at poos of 12, unless there's a lot ot help in make-up for the success disparity like very low TNs, a difference of 12 successes (assuming the chart isn't fixed) between 9 and 8 is a tad ludicrous, since unless you have very low TNs at that tier, you're in effect getting flat out as many successes as their pool maxes out to on vaverage. This only exapserates just one Scale less than that.<br /> <br /> If that's the goal, it does it, but I do kind of wonder if the want to use the Fibonacci sequence is the best way to go save for a very limitted range that seems to break in half once you hit about 8+ for actual gamability.<br /> <br /> Which note is actually my main thing on the system and worries on being all post-modern and such. I am curious how wounds are handled, as that might impact things as well. As long as it's not like Exalted 2e rocket tag or nWoD's mugging simulator I'm sure things will end up well in trying to replicate what the games are trying to be in a fight at least and there seems to be enough emphasis on non-combat to make the success scale seem pretty great to me for those things.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Why roll? Chases. There are environmental considerations. The formula also happens to plug into systems for vehicle speeds. The muddled order of operations is noted.<br /> <br /> 2) The Intensity formula may change, since it was imposed after the fact and doesn't really match. I talked to Neall about this just last night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":164,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","user":"Malcolm","date":". 06-19-2015, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T07:45:45-07:00","id":560816,"title":"","content":"After getting some answers to my question, about opinion on focus I thnk I can ask. Is there something truly good, not just potenitally interesting about the mechanic, because response seems to be very meh at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T08:02:10-07:00","id":560845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=560496#post560496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The movement pool is weird to me since I don't know why it it has to be x2 after the pool. IN part since I'm not sure the order of operations ((Agiltiy + Athletics) x 2 or Agility + (Athletics x2)) and why the doubling of successes for Speed. Or what the fuck ou do wiht a Difficulty 0 roll normally unless there's environmental stuff after that I guess. I might just have missed something on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You double it, not to determine your pool but the distance you can travel in a turn without rolling. So Finesse 2 + Athletics 2 allows for 8 yards (sixteen if you give up your action). You only roll when faced with a barrier though the dicepool could change based on said barrier.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T08:15:05-07:00","id":560861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=560816#post560816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After getting some answers to my question, about opinion on focus I thnk I can ask. Is there something truly good, not just potenitally interesting about the mechanic, because response seems to be very meh at best.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for your contributions! I note that you feel so strongly about this that your entire posting history is only to threads about Sardonyx, and only consists of opinions like this one. Keep on trucking!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T08:24:36-07:00","id":560864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=560704#post560704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird. I never saw Aeon as dark, or at least any darker than the real world. My games always had plenty of shiny space cities and high tech solutions, maybe to differentiate it from the Shadowrun games we played, which were filled with constant betrayals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear ya - I came to Aeon specifically because I was done with the WoD.<br /> <br /> There were definitely those shiny elements in my games too - but I embraced things like Huang Marr, political infighting between the orders, Aeon overreaching, discord in Europe, fascism in the FSA, and so on as well. The not-quite-yet-post-apocalyptic nature of much of the setting really did it for me and felt more plausible than more a more upbeat future. I toned down the shiny stuff, but only a little. Not saying I ran grim-dark as that wasn't the case, but a superhero game Aeon 'aint. Intense? Sure. Dangerous? Definitely. If I finished a campaign with the players wondering how on earth their characters survived and deep sense of satisfaction at, finally, ending the bad guys, then that was a job well done. Also, those games are the ones reminisced about FAR more than anything else I've ever chosen to GM.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=560704#post560704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having used a similar system in a Fate campaign or two, I agree that this form of initiative is divorced from the abilities of the characters. However, it does allow the players significantly more control over the pace of the conflict, so it doesn't feel arbitrary. In practice, you're passing the spotlight to the next logical player and setting up combos to take down the bad guys.<br /> <br /> In the campaigns in which I've used / experienced the &quot;players choose who goes next&quot; initiative, we have a quiet player, a casual player, and a player who often forgets which floor the party is on. These players were not the last picked, because the more active/aggressive players were the ones doing the picking, and they'd chose the character that made the most sense to go next. If the coolest thing to happen right now would be for the brick to throw a barrel to distract the goon squad, setting up the others in the party to pick them off with blasters, then you hand the initiative to the brick, regardless of the activity level of the player.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've done similar too but had mixed results, especially with players that don't always work well together. Also, I intensively dislike the meta nature of that level of strategic play, for example handing over to the brick because that's collectively a logical what the PC's need next. Its a personal preference, and something I am highly unlikely to ever use again. I happily acknowledge that some people love this stuff, I'm just not one of them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T15:12:16-07:00","id":561263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=560726#post560726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) Why roll? Chases. There are environmental considerations. The formula also happens to plug into systems for vehicle speeds. The muddle order of operations is noted.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We really need to see this chase and vehicle systems you are talking about to get a better clue about how things are supposed to work. That said, something occurs to me.<br /> <br /> First of all, the initiative roll doesn't really seem very important on the surface. It's mostly going to be determining if it's an NPC or a PC who goes very first in the turn, and that seems to be it. You aren't going to have situations of everyone dog-piling on the bad guy or all the bad guys getting the drop on the PC who rolled crap. That's probably good.<br /> <br /> What concerns me here is what it means for the director. Let's say I'm running a scene. I've got a big bad evil mastermind, along with one of his faithful lieutenants and a smattering of goons. I've also got both some helpful NPCs in the form of the cops trying to give the PCs some cover/support fire, and some hapless victims trying to get away. Now I could give everybody the same initiative, but that would be tricky across multiple traits, and it would mean the NPC turn would be really long and weirdly sandwiched - it just doesn't fit good timing. So I want to separate everyone out into five or so groups - the boss, the lieutenant, the goons, the cops, and the hostages. Now to do this, I'm going to have to calculate a fairly tricky dice-pool - I have to compare two different scores, then add, factor in environment/modifiers, then roll, then record and I have to do it five times. That is honestly kind of a drag. Now if it was something like say, 1d10+Cunning, what I could do is just roll five dice, assign them to each group, and be good to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T15:14:29-07:00","id":561265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=560864#post560864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I've done similar too but had mixed results, especially with players that don't always work well together. Also, I intensively dislike the meta nature of that level of strategic play, for example handing over to the brick because that's collectively a logical what the PC's need next. Its a personal preference, and something I am highly unlikely to ever use again. I happily acknowledge that some people love this stuff, I'm just not one of them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me like a decent model for a team that will typically have this kind of thing worked out in advance. But I see what you are saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T15:47:33-07:00","id":561296,"title":"","content":"The red and black pools are there to promote pacing, right? So how about, instead of forcing a back-and-forth between players and npcs, you use Momentum to reward passing the action back and forth? If you choose to have the players all act at once, you can; but once the npcs start to act, they'll have a lot of Momentum to work with. <br /> <br /> My main problem with the &quot;passing the baton&quot; approach described here is that it strikes me as a logistical nightmare, as everyone needs to keep track of who has already acted this round and who hasn't. Maybe give everyone a token at the start of each round, and require everypne to &quot;spend&quot; their token to act. As long as you have an &quot;action token&quot;, you have the ability to act. Or something like that\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T21:42:25-07:00","id":561552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=561296#post561296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main problem with the &quot;passing the baton&quot; approach described here is that it strikes me as a logistical nightmare, as everyone needs to keep track of who has already acted this round and who hasn't. Maybe give everyone a token at the start of each round, and require everyone to &quot;spend&quot; their token to act. As long as you have an &quot;action token&quot;, you have the ability to act. Or something like that\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>For small groups, it's probably not too much of an issue. For large groups, you could just have note cards that say &quot;Ready&quot; and &quot;Done&quot;, or something similar, and simply flip them back and forth as needed. I use that approach for keeping track of who has already activated in <b>Super Dungeon Explore</b>, which has a shockingly similar initiative system now that I think about it, and it works fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T05:27:34-07:00","id":561804,"title":"","content":"Still, for a game that wants to be fast, we're tracking a lot of variables here.<br /> <br /> I like tokens as a player aid for all manner of things. But there is a limit to what a lot of people want to have to pay attention to","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T06:08:01-07:00","id":561823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=561804#post561804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, for a game that wants to be fast, we're tracking a lot of variables here.<br /> <br /> I like tokens as a player aid for all manner of things. But there is a limit to what a lot of people want to have to pay attention to</div> </div> </div> </div>It is another layer, but I do think it is swingy enough without focus. Now I see it like this.<br /> <br /> 1. Init roll- Who goes first and who gets focus. Init tokens of all players are green.<br /> 2. First guy goes(has action token).- Action I hope one roll of maximum 14 dice against number on his sheet/stats+ Scale if applicable. Possibly invoked exotic dice effect, which should be rare.<br /> 3. Action happens. First guy says who goes after him(gives action token) and flips init token to red. Enemy party goes<br /> 4. Repeat until round ends- everyone init token is red. New round switch tokens new init roll?????<br /> <br /> Then there is tracing of life and potential debuffs and similar things.<br /> <br /> Focus adds additional multiround token and you must be ready to jump in, on moments notice. It does add layer of bookkeeping.<br /> <br /> This setup as I see it needs very quick initiative roll, so you do not have a lot of dead time as Director rolls his dice. Experience suggest rules for separating Director character into initiative group is very needed and this style will not do well with many individual opponents- It will get slightly boring and dead time will increase swiftly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6491,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","user":"zorb42","date":". 06-20-2015, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T07:52:08-07:00","id":561905,"title":"","content":"I don't even know if action tokens are necessary. Just flip over your character sheet. When everyone is flipped, flip them back and start a new round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T12:59:08-07:00","id":562161,"title":"","content":"For perspective, the order of actions system in Sardonyx is something I use in all my games now, and not because I felt it was super-clever (okay, I do think it's kind of clever though) but because it's the laziest possible system. It's much, much simpler than traditional initiative. Instead of a countdown I just go. &quot;And this guy goes. Okay Steve, who goes next?&quot; And Steve says &quot;Katrina.&quot; That is literally it. The person in focus just says, &quot;I wanna go now.&quot; I can't remember any confusion over whether everybody went ever lasting longer than three seconds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":164,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","user":"Malcolm","date":". 06-20-2015, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T17:20:46-07:00","id":562378,"title":"","content":"Yeah, most groups will only have three or four players. I don't think that's so many that there'll be any confusion over who's gone and who hasn't in a given round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T00:00:59-07:00","id":562714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=562378#post562378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, most groups will only have three or four players. I don't think that's so many that there'll be any confusion over who's gone and who hasn't in a given round.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as a common noob. It does get confusing and while confusion is never long lasting. It does happen. Problem is keeping track of whole battle, not just players, which does increase the load from three to much more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T01:28:22-07:00","id":562741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=562161#post562161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For perspective, the order of actions system in Sardonyx is something I use in all my games now, and not because I felt it was super-clever (okay, I do think it's kind of clever though) but because it's the laziest possible system. It's much, much simpler than traditional initiative. Instead of a countdown I just go. &quot;And this guy goes. Okay Steve, who goes next?&quot; And Steve says &quot;Katrina.&quot; That is literally it. The person in focus just says, &quot;I wanna go now.&quot; I can't remember any confusion over whether everybody went ever lasting longer than three seconds.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is an interesting system, but it's not necessarily a system which I feel that most groups would use naturally. Just have regular initiative order, roll it andfigure out who goes when. Then you can have faster characters going first and slower characters going last, as God intended <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T10:12:29-07:00","id":563090,"title":"","content":"Considering that the engine seems to be putting a lot of emphasis (at least on the tactics of the game) on teamwork on cooperation, this style of initiative is often beneficial. The &quot;everyone goes in order of fastest to slowest&quot; is simple in an intuitive sense, but always a pain in the ass from the stand point of trying to encourage group tactical thinking. The classic style of fast-to-slow generally ends up forcing you to pick between tactics that only work based on that order, or force you to devalue fast characters by forcing them to wait until the NPCs go so that they can act with the slower PCs.<br /> <br /> To pull an example from Marvel, if my team has Quicksilver (high init), Colossus (low init), and Wolverine (medium init), with Scarlet Witch getting the focus baton, Quicksilver goes first, sets up Colossus, who can then fastball special Wolverine, and the Scarlet Witch can use her Focus status to step in and Hex up the enemies for Wolverine to fly past the mooks and claw the big bad.<br /> <br /> In a classic init style, Quicksilver basically adds nothing to this, or is basically there to try to pick off some mooks. Wolverine has to delay past Colossus, and Colossus past the Scarlet Witch, so she can cast her Hex, then Colossus can hurl Wolverine at the enemy. And all the speedier enemies got to go in the meantime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T10:33:23-07:00","id":563106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=562378#post562378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, most groups will only have three or four players. I don't think that's so many that there'll be any confusion over who's gone and who hasn't in a given round.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I have been one of the most &quot;rah rah&quot; about Sardonyx, but this reaction does <i>not</i> please me. I have five adults and two <i>children</i> in the group I run. Should I not use Sardonyx for them?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T10:57:39-07:00","id":563114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=562161#post562161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For perspective, the order of actions system in Sardonyx is something I use in all my games now, and not because I felt it was super-clever (okay, I do think it's kind of clever though) but because it's the laziest possible system. It's much, much simpler than traditional initiative. Instead of a countdown I just go. &quot;And this guy goes. Okay Steve, who goes next?&quot; And Steve says &quot;Katrina.&quot; That is literally it. The person in focus just says, &quot;I wanna go now.&quot; I can't remember any confusion over whether everybody went ever lasting longer than three seconds.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Lazy is God at the Gaming Table (15 year veteran)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Aeon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=563106#post563106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I have been one of the most &quot;rah rah&quot; about Sardonyx, but this reaction does <i>not</i> please me. I have five adults and two <i>children</i> in the group I run. Should I not use Sardonyx for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>How young? I have a ten year old BEGGING to play, and while my core group is out of bounds, I've been thinking about allowing her to play with her mom and a friend.<br /> <br /> Also, as a guy who runs a game for 6-7 players I don't see this system as being any more hectic as the old tic system which was 'neat' but hell on the nerves. I think Ian was speaking hypothetically as he doesn't run a large game. Malcom's is a better response.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":256,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","user":"Gnomish American","date":". 06-21-2015, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T10:59:39-07:00","id":563117,"title":"","content":"It just means you're probably going to have to work a bit harder on your table-organization when high action scenes breaks out? I think you're taking Ian's comment pretty harshly. He's just saying what they consider the target group size is; not some weird judgement on the &quot;best&quot; group size.<br /> <br /> I mean, there's pretty much true regardless. I've never seen any initiative system that actually scales seamlessly for any number of players. The more players, the more most (I'd say all, but I'll acknowledge the possibility of some LARP or similar systems that are actually better in the reverse) RPGs require the group to do things to keep the order straight.<br /> <br /> Running the classic fast-to-slow with twenty characters/groups of mooks (especially when the range of inits is low) takes a lot more work than when you have six characters/groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T12:22:47-07:00","id":563280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Aeon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=563106#post563106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I have been one of the most &quot;rah rah&quot; about Sardonyx, but this reaction does <i>not</i> please me. I have five adults and two <i>children</i> in the group I run. Should I not use Sardonyx for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal opinion is you shouldn't run anything with that many people, but if you guys like it, then it's gravy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T16:03:45-07:00","id":563470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Aeon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=563106#post563106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I have been one of the most &quot;rah rah&quot; about Sardonyx, but this reaction does <i>not</i> please me. I have five adults and two <i>children</i> in the group I run. Should I not use Sardonyx for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said &quot;Sardonyx should only be used for games of X size or below&quot; or anything similar to that. There's no reason whatsoever you can't run Sardonyx with a larger group, and I am not telling you you can't or shouldn't.<br /> <br /> I simply said that, for your average group size, keeping track of who has and hasn't gone in a round shouldn't be challenging enough that you need some sort of extra tracker. Maybe your group does need a tracker. Maybe you can still keep track of it easily with a game of that size without a tracker. I've run a group with over a dozen people before and I handled this with a simple &quot;who still needs to go this round?&quot; and it worked fine. Your mileage may vary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T18:34:17-07:00","id":563612,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping for Edges next teaser, but maybe we will see what they did to replace Health Boxes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T06:39:36-07:00","id":564052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Aeon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=563106#post563106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I have been one of the most &quot;rah rah&quot; about Sardonyx, but this reaction does <i>not</i> please me. I have five adults and two <i>children</i> in the group I run. Should I not use Sardonyx for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>You should be fine, though I recommend tokens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T09:30:15-07:00","id":564193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=563612#post563612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping for Edges next teaser, but maybe we will see what they did to replace Health Boxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edges? Did I miss something?<br /> <br /> Edit: I found it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":256,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","user":"Gnomish American","date":". 06-22-2015, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T10:27:32-07:00","id":564254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=563114#post563114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How young? I have a ten year old BEGGING to play, and while my core group is out of bounds, I've been thinking about allowing her to play with her mom and a friend.</div> </div> </div> </div>They started at ten each, though yes, I <i>strongly</i> recommend having a parent there. Both parents are part of my group, and I check with them before introducing darker stuff. Funnily enough, the older one started because she was crazy for the Percy Jackson books, and <i>had</i> to play a Scion of Poseidon. (Amusingly, she didn't otherwise resemble Percy -- too hyper. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) It was actually kind of fun. I don't expect to run Scion again -- it was a very complete game -- but we keep circling a pulp adventure setting, and I love the heck out of Adventure!, so...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T12:54:41-07:00","id":564462,"title":"","content":"I am the parent, but her mom showed interest in the game as well. Though like the rest of my group she refuses to play 1st edition. Its funny how a game can be so loved and so disliked by the same people at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T12:57:33-07:00","id":564467,"title":"","content":"So... anyone else using the spoilers to build an ad hoc character sheet? Am I alone in my obsession?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T20:58:23-07:00","id":564970,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to picture what it's going to look like, myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T21:39:36-07:00","id":564985,"title":"","content":"Mine is pretty much designed to look like first ed (for now) I just know that Beast and the other games that came out through kickstarter didn't have sheets so I'm building it from scratch, (I tried using the original, but the file was... less then helpful. So I built another and then took the graphics from other sheets <i>AND</i> learned some neat tricks. My game is gonna be based on America so I used the background of the American Pantheon (its very bright). I AM thinking about putting the skills down the side ala NWOD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T06:02:15-07:00","id":565279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=564970#post564970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to picture what it's going to look like, myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Horizontal, if I get my druthers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T08:09:54-07:00","id":565420,"title":"","content":"I'd just like to say, there's one thing I really want to see in the sardonyx system games, although it's not really a system thing so much as a &quot;not locked into a specific time or timeline&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> If there are any fallen or lost groups that are important to the lore or setting of the game, like Chitra Bhanu, like the White Howlers and Bunyip in wwta, etc., that their powers, special skills, unique weaknesses, everything needed to still play them or use them as NPCs/villains, be included at least as an appendix or part of the storyteller section.<br /> <br /> It took twenty years to get rules to play a pure White Howler and we never did get real rules for quantikinetics. It just always bothered me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":509,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","user":"TiwazTyrsfist","date":".  Typo 06-23-2015, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T11:14:52-07:00","id":565585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=565420#post565420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd just like to say, there's one thing I really want to see in the sardonyx system games, although it's not really a system thing so much as a &quot;not locked into a specific time or timeline&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> If there are any fallen or lost groups that are important to the lore or setting of the game, like Chitra Bhanu, like the White Howlers and Bunyip in wwta, etc., that their powers, special skills, unique weaknesses, everything needed to still play them or use them as NPCs/villains, be included at least as an appendix or part of the storyteller section.<br /> <br /> It took twenty years to get rules to play a pure White Howler and we never did get real rules for quantikinetics. It just always bothered me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree in general sense, but I do consider Quantakinetics to be somewhat special case. You really need eximorph fluff hard done and their themes set in stone, before you write something, that is supposed to mimic them.<br /> <br /> Imo it might be cool to take Quantakinetics as Doyen see the quantum and make them antipsions, but that is just an idea.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T12:10:03-07:00","id":565602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=565279#post565279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Horizontal, if I get my druthers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Attributes down the left side, skills in the middle advantages to the right? Name/player across the top or... oh, Im gonna see what I can do on mine.<br /> <br /> Being a dork I was tinkering and had some success with horizontal, and was even able to keep the 1st edition graphics on the sheet (some of them) fun fact: easiest way to group the attributes was by arena AND it allowed me to put in 12 lines for &quot;common rolls&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":256,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","user":"Gnomish American","date":".  Acted like a dork. 06-23-2015, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T13:53:50-07:00","id":565732,"title":"","content":"DOOD!!! Did y'all even notice its TYR's Day!!!! (Give us what we want and we'll go away)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T14:16:52-07:00","id":565751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbco