Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T14:40:32-08:00","id":759362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=666933#post666933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> I actually grew rather fond of Sardonyx, but I lapse into using it when I shouldn't - it's Storypath now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you there. I have a hard time not calling it Sardonyx. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1360-fortinbras","name":"Fortinbras","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T04:05:09-08:00","id":759877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=757384#post757384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing yet. We will likely get some small rules spoilers next year just before convention season gets going again and all three of the staff vanish into the ether again. Hopefully looking to Kickstart by late 2017 for Trinity Core/Aeon, then backer pdf dropping early 2019, with the print copy being just in time for Christmas, 2020.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is a very bleak outlook. I wouldn't think it would take that long. I was hoping to use it for a Trinity game next year. Old rules it is then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T05:19:05-08:00","id":759909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>karpomatic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=759877#post759877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a very bleak outlook. I wouldn't think it would take that long.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not an unrealistic timeline for a project of this size. The original AEON took just 10 months, but that was fast-tracked, and was for a single book (Aberrant was released 2 years after that, and Adventure 2 years after that).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T05:46:24-08:00","id":759925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=759909#post759909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not an unrealistic timeline for a project of this size. The original AEON took just 10 months, but that was fast-tracked, and was for a single book (Aberrant was released 2 years after that, and Adventure 2 years after that).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would consider it very unrealistic. 2020 for the first book?! That's considerably longer than Exalted3 took and Exalted was practically rewritten from scratch during its production.<br /> <br /> The TC core's production was put on hold until the Storypath system was completed, which it nearly is. Assuming it doesn't take much longer, there's every reason to expect the core to drop in 2016.<br /> <br /> I suspect Wolfgar was being sarcastic as a way of grumbling about existing delays, and not giving an actual prediction based on anything. No one's more frustrated than I am about how long this has taken, I assure you, but that's no reason to spread misinformation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T06:06:21-08:00","id":759941,"title":"","content":"I am chomping at the bit for this new core rule book to appear. I've been saving money in PayPal for it for months now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Man's unfailing capacity to believe what he prefers to be true rather than what the evidence shows to be likely and possible has always astounded me. We long for a caring Universe which will save us from our childish mistakes, and in the face of mountains of evidence to the contrary we will pin all our hopes on the slimmest of doubts. God has not been proven not to exist, therefore he must exist.</i> <b>--Academician Prokhor Zakharov</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3246-galaxy-master-zhad","name":"Galaxy Master Zhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T19:28:25-08:00","id":760410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=759925#post759925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would consider it very unrealistic. 2020 for the first book?! That's considerably longer than Exalted3 took and Exalted was practically rewritten from scratch during its production.<br /> <br /> The TC core's production was put on hold until the Storypath system was completed, which it nearly is. Assuming it doesn't take much longer, there's every reason to expect the core to drop in 2016.<br /> <br /> I suspect Wolfgar was being sarcastic as a way of grumbling about existing delays, and not giving an actual prediction based on anything. No one's more frustrated than I am about how long this has taken, I assure you, but that's no reason to spread misinformation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am trolling, but no grumbling here. The fact of the matter is the answer is always &quot;It will happen when it happens&quot; and really trying to set anything like a date or even the vaguest expectation seems to be an invitation to disappointment. Every step in the process will seem longer than it should, and that isn't factoring in the numerous disasters that can and probably will happen, from every third word in the first printing being changed to &quot;BORT&quot; to Neil's torso dissolving during an allergic reaction. Setting up expectations that will be shattered is just going to make us needlessly angry, and make the creators needlessly stressed out and upset. Seriously, this should be a fun thing for all of us. I apologize if my dark amusement seems to be taken too seriously.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T19:39:22-08:00","id":760415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Galaxy Master Zhad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=759941#post759941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am chomping at the bit for this new core rule book to appear. I've been saving money in PayPal for it for months now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep saving. We all want to be a part of the &quot;Make Ian wear funny hats for the entirety of the publishing process&quot; reward tier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T16:09:02-08:00","id":761010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=759925#post759925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would consider it very unrealistic. 2020 for the first book?! That's considerably longer than Exalted3 took and Exalted was practically rewritten from scratch during its production.<br /> <br /> The TC core's production was put on hold until the Storypath system was completed, which it nearly is. Assuming it doesn't take much longer, there's every reason to expect the core to drop in 2016.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make me happy. It would make me even happier to know when Aberrant is likely to happen <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And the paroxysms of joy will be real if the... odd... formatting of the original books was perhaps... left by the wayside and made to look more like a traditional OPP book ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T16:38:05-08:00","id":761033,"title":"","content":"I would expect Aberrant roughly a year after Aeon and the core drop, then Adventure!, and then Anima, roughly, although it might go faster or slower depending on how well things go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T06:18:44-08:00","id":761423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=759925#post759925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would consider it very unrealistic. 2020 for the first book?! That's considerably longer than Exalted3 took and Exalted was practically rewritten from scratch during its production.<br /> <br /> The TC core's production was put on hold until the Storypath system was completed, which it nearly is. Assuming it doesn't take much longer, there's every reason to expect the core to drop in 2016.<br /> <br /> I suspect Wolfgar was being sarcastic as a way of grumbling about existing delays, and not giving an actual prediction based on anything. No one's more frustrated than I am about how long this has taken, I assure you, but that's no reason to spread misinformation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ian, you're operating with information that the rest of us don't have. Just looking at the publicly available history, 2020 for a print version of Aeon doesn't seem unreasonable, so calling it &quot;misinformation&quot; seems harsh.<br /> <br /> Most OPP KS projects appear to have a 10-12 month gap between &quot;end of KS&quot; and &quot;all books shipped.&quot; D&amp;D Next's dev period took nearly 2 years, once it entered public playtest. We're in November, so the earliest start date for the entire process would be logically January 2016. Add 3 years, and that's January 2019 for the print version of Aeon (which, admittedly isn't the &quot;first&quot; book, but it's the first of the Trinity that we're all eagerly awaiting). And since this is the hobby games industry, delays of a year aren't uncommon, so: 2020.<br /> <br /> If you believe the core book will be released in 2016, excellent! I'm glad to hear it, and am happy to revise my expectations. <br /> <br /> You're under no obligation to discuss the sausage-making, of course, but if you want to update my timeline with your knowledge, I'd happily spread the correct information.<br /> <br /> Thanks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T06:24:59-08:00","id":761428,"title":"","content":"I was just hoping the teasers would pick back up to keep us interested. They were coming steady for a few weeks there then dropped off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T06:53:57-08:00","id":761442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=761423#post761423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're under no obligation to discuss the sausage-making, of course, but if you want to update my timeline with your knowledge, I'd happily spread the correct information.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, you know, it'll get here when it gets here. Speculation is all good and well, I'm all for it generally, but I've noticed people do tend to get a little........unintentionally demanding......when it comes to things like timescale estimates. I've taken the approach of setting my expectations to 'whenever they finally tell us its ready, is when its ready'. Much easier <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T09:22:27-08:00","id":761549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=761442#post761442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or, you know, it'll get here when it gets here. Speculation is all good and well, I'm all for it generally, but I've noticed people do tend to get a little........unintentionally demanding......when it comes to things like timescale estimates. I've taken the approach of setting my expectations to 'whenever they finally tell us its ready, is when its ready'. Much easier <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think anyone's been demanding of a timescale estimate -- just good old fashioned enthusiasm.<br /> <br /> And a &quot;when it's ready&quot; attitude is fine for folks who are very likely to buy into the line no matter the form or release date. But stuff like timelines and sneak peeks build anticipation, anticipation builds engagement, and engagement makes a larger player base. <br /> <br /> IMO, YMMV, etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T10:46:50-08:00","id":761600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=761010#post761010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the paroxysms of joy will be real if the... odd... formatting of the original books was perhaps... left by the wayside and made to look more like a traditional OPP book ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, with the exception of the Cavaliers of Mars quickstart, all we've seen in the last almost-four years are <i>traditional White Wolf books</i>. We have yet to determine if an Onyx Path book looks much different. (:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T10:59:26-08:00","id":761606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=761423#post761423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ian, you're operating with information that the rest of us don't have. Just looking at the publicly available history, 2020 for a print version of Aeon doesn't seem unreasonable, so calling it &quot;misinformation&quot; seems harsh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Onyx Path has been around for for almost four years now. 2020 is five years away. Exalted has been our most famously late delivery, but &quot;only&quot; two years. So yes, I would call an estimate of five more years to be unreasonable, given our existing track record.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most OPP KS projects appear to have a 10-12 month gap between &quot;end of KS&quot; and &quot;all books shipped.&quot; </div> </div> </div>You're conflating a Kickstarter deluxe printing with &quot;print book.&quot; The PoD will doubtless be available well before the KS deluxe copy is delivered.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T12:30:37-08:00","id":761661,"title":"","content":"Ian, thanks for the update. Looking forward to more peeks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T13:03:17-08:00","id":761670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=761549#post761549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But stuff like timelines and sneak peeks build anticipation, anticipation builds engagement, and engagement makes a larger player base.<br /> IMO, YMMV, etc</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I agree (well, except on timescales). However I've had conversations with people whose attitude has gone from anticipation to excitement to frustration around the new TC already because it (I quote) &quot;should be done already&quot;. I think sneak peaks, teasers and so on are great though - I just think timescale estimates tend to feed frustrations. Keep it vague until its near done, don't give any estimates, but tease from time to time so we know it isn't dead and I'm good until you're ready to announce its coming in a month or something. But, like you said IMO, YMMV, etc <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":232,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","user":"CHILL","date":".  damn you autocorrect 11-09-2015, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T14:44:40-08:00","id":761729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=761606#post761606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're conflating a Kickstarter deluxe printing with &quot;print book.&quot; The PoD will doubtless be available well before the KS deluxe copy is delivered.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, and I mean this politely and respectfully as possible, people do usually kick in for the deluxe book, not a chance to buy the same book twice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T14:53:20-08:00","id":761737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=761423#post761423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ian, you're operating with information that the rest of us don't have. Just looking at the publicly available history, 2020 for a print version of Aeon doesn't seem unreasonable, so calling it &quot;misinformation&quot; seems harsh.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is misinformation in this case, as I have only mild personal experience to base such a thing on, and certainly nothing approaching reliable insider experience or even intimate familiarity with the process from the publisher side.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T19:07:57-08:00","id":761935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=761600#post761600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interestingly, with the exception of the Cavaliers of Mars quickstart, all we've seen in the last almost-four years are <i>traditional White Wolf books</i>. We have yet to determine if an Onyx Path book looks much different. (:</div> </div> </div> </div>Traditional White Wolf book then :P They're synonyms in my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T00:29:30-08:00","id":762059,"title":"","content":"From today's Monday Meeting notes, this happened almost exactly four years ago, after Black Wednesday but before Onyx Path:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/trinity-texted-to-ian.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=761729#post761729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, and I mean this politely and respectfully as possible, people do usually kick in for the deluxe book, not a chance to buy the same book twice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, people who pledge on Kickstarter are usually after a deluxe book. But we're talking &quot;when will a printed book be out,&quot; which is Kickstarter-independent. Not everyone's going to jump in on the KS, after all.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T04:47:13-08:00","id":762197,"title":"","content":"My friends love Exalted. So I am running Exalted 3rd edition for them since they MUST play this game.<br /> I love the NWoD so I am running a game of it so that they can get familiar with it until they can run a game of it.<br /> When Aeoniverse 2nd drops, I am shoving the book into my friend's hands and go &quot;READ THIS. RUN IT.&quot; and use guilt from the games I am running to get them to do it.<br /> The point of mentioning this is that, for some of us, the gameline was too little and we want more. We loved it the first time around, lumps and wonky mechanics and all, and want it to come back all chromed up and sleeked out. Any spoilers will be devoured and analyzed. When the KS hits, it will get it's funding. Does it matter how long it takes? Well for those of us who sat through Exalted 3rd edition from the KS until it's publication, then we can also wait for Aeoniverse to show up once more. <br /> Patience will just build up the excitement for when it comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T09:36:25-08:00","id":762370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=762059#post762059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From today's Monday Meeting notes, this happened almost exactly four years ago, after Black Wednesday but before Onyx Path:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/trinity-texted-to-ian.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, people who pledge on Kickstarter are usually after a deluxe book. But we're talking &quot;when will a printed book be out,&quot; which is Kickstarter-independent. Not everyone's going to jump in on the KS, after all.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its so cool that he remembered that message to you, Ian. <br /> <br /> I can say that the Trinity trilogy Kickstarters will be the first ones that I will be going for the deluxe books. I am almost totally digital at the table but these games are my absolute favorites. I must have the books on my shelf with the old editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T15:49:05-08:00","id":762669,"title":"","content":"I have yet to find a good solution as far as PDF for table-use is concerned. Mostly I'm just looking forward to getting to see the new rule sand pick everything to pieces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T15:56:09-08:00","id":763546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=762669#post762669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have yet to find a good solution as far as PDF for table-use is concerned. Mostly I'm just looking forward to getting to see the new rule sand pick everything to pieces.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've found the all-too-easy distraction provided by laptops, tablets and phones at the gaming table is <b><i>way</i></b> more trouble than they're worth. I like digital copies for between-session reading and if I ever have to do online gaming (bleh), but at the table a physical book or two is enough for me.<br /> <br /> <i>Now </i><i>put your damn phone away / get off my lawn, young 'uns! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T16:41:58-08:00","id":763580,"title":"","content":"Back in my day we had Mage arguments just to keep the children warm!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T17:07:00-08:00","id":764530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=763580#post763580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back in my day we had Mage arguments just to keep the children warm!</div> </div> </div> </div>....... children now all grown up, same Mage arguments still going, by any chance? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T19:58:12-08:00","id":764648,"title":"","content":"Don't know. We all had to run out when the house caught fire and the earth around it turned to molten slag and sunk below the crust, but the pit appears to still be giving off enough heat for Brucato to dance around it naked with no visible signs of shrinkage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T04:50:57-08:00","id":775388,"title":"","content":"After rereading the teasers, I think I have a handle on the damage system. There's a Survival Trick that says you only get 'Taken Out' if your attacker scores 7 successes, leading me to believe that it normally takes 5 or 6 successes. For fewer successes you can inflict Impairment or Bleeding conditions (mentioned under Medicine), which weaken an enemy (maybe Impairments add difficulty, not sure what Bleeding would do mechanically). Eventually, you soften up your enemy enough to take them out. I'm guessing different weapons can inflict different conditions (blades and guns cause Bleeding, bludgeons might stun or cripple limbs). Cool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/820-gyre","name":"gyre","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T12:12:53-08:00","id":775576,"title":"","content":"If you want to see existing game systems that use Condition-based damage systems, check out \u201cMutants and Masterminds\u201d and \u201cFate\u201d. Though note that both effectively hide a damage track of sorts underneath, as they limit how many of each kind of impairment you're allowed to have before you're forced to escalate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T07:59:17-08:00","id":793091,"title":"","content":"Somewhat unrelated question - how many pages have all the compiled teasers so far? Is there any place where one may get them together?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T07:04:57-08:00","id":794800,"title":"","content":"There is a link in Chill's signature that will take you to the compiled spoiler list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T15:15:42-08:00","id":797036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>karpomatic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=794800#post794800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a link in Chill's signature that will take you to the compiled spoiler list.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that - it's nice but more of a list of commentaries and possible setting spoilers on the part of the Devs.<br /> <br /> I was thinking more of a file with all the sketchy mechanics info we got so far from the public teasers together in one place, actually.<br /> A partial rough draft of sorts, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T15:47:56-08:00","id":798438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=797036#post797036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking more of a file with all the sketchy mechanics info we got so far from the public teasers together in one place, actually.<br /> A partial rough draft of sorts, so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's only been a couple teasers, so I don't think there's been a need to collate yet. Of course, there's nothing stopping anyone collating them and dumping them in a Google Doc or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T16:56:55-08:00","id":798477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=798438#post798438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's only been a couple teasers, so I don't think there's been a need to collate yet. Of course, there's nothing stopping anyone collating them and dumping them in a Google Doc or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last i checked, you get about 50 pages if you collate the 3 public teasers together. Still smallish, but getting interesting i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}